// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測/IELTS/TOEFL Topic 14
window.I14_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"News & Journalism 新聞與新聞業","cards":[{"w":"journalism","p":"n.","d":"the work of collecting and writing news","c":"新聞業；新聞工作","s":"My cousin studied journalism at university, and now she writes stories about local problems for an online newspaper.","t":"我的表姊在大學主修新聞學，現在她為一家線上報紙撰寫關於地方問題的報導。"},{"w":"journalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes or reports the news","c":"記者；新聞工作者","s":"The journalist waited outside the hospital for hours, but the doctors refused to answer any of her questions.","t":"那位記者在醫院外等了好幾個小時，但醫生們拒絕回答她的任何問題。"},{"w":"reporter","p":"n.","d":"a person who finds and tells news stories","c":"記者；採訪員","s":"A young reporter was sent to cover the typhoon, so he stood in the rain and described the damage on live TV.","t":"一位年輕的記者被派去報導颱風，所以他站在雨中，在電視直播上描述災情。"},{"w":"correspondent","p":"n.","d":"a journalist who reports from a particular place or topic","c":"特派員；通訊記者","s":"The BBC's correspondent in Tokyo has lived in Japan for ten years, so she understands the local culture very well.","t":"英國廣播公司駐東京的特派員已經在日本住了十年，所以她非常了解當地文化。"},{"w":"editor","p":"n.","d":"a person who checks and decides what is published","c":"編輯；主編","s":"The editor asked me to cut my article from 1,000 words to 600, because there was not enough space on the page.","t":"編輯要求我把文章從一千字刪到六百字，因為版面上沒有足夠的空間。"},{"w":"editorial","p":"n.","d":"a newspaper article giving the paper's opinion","c":"社論","s":"Today's editorial criticises the government's new housing plan, and many readers have written letters to agree with it.","t":"今天的社論批評政府的新住宅計畫，而許多讀者寫信表示贊同。"},{"w":"headline","p":"n.","d":"the title of a news story in large letters","c":"新聞標題；頭條","s":"The headline said that prices would double, but when I read the whole article, the real increase was only five percent.","t":"那則標題說價格會翻倍，但當我讀完整篇文章時，實際漲幅只有百分之五。"},{"w":"front page","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first page of a newspaper with the main news","c":"頭版","s":"The photo of the flooded village appeared on the front page of every newspaper, so the whole country saw it the next morning.","t":"那張被淹沒村莊的照片出現在每份報紙的頭版上，所以隔天早上全國的人都看到了。"},{"w":"newspaper","p":"n.","d":"printed pages of news published daily or weekly","c":"報紙","s":"My grandfather still buys a paper newspaper every morning, although most of his friends now read the news on their phones.","t":"我爺爺每天早上仍然買一份紙本報紙，儘管他大部分朋友現在都用手機看新聞。"},{"w":"newsroom","p":"n.","d":"the office where journalists prepare the news","c":"新聞編輯室","s":"The newsroom was very busy on election night, and nobody went home until all the results had been reported.","t":"選舉當晚新聞編輯室非常忙碌，直到所有結果都報導完之前沒有人回家。"},{"w":"press conference","p":"n.phr.","d":"a meeting where someone answers reporters' questions","c":"記者會","s":"The mayor held a press conference after the fire, but he left quickly because reporters kept asking difficult questions.","t":"市長在火災後召開了記者會，但他很快就離開了，因為記者們一直問困難的問題。"},{"w":"press release","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official statement given to journalists","c":"新聞稿","s":"The company sent out a press release about its new phone, and dozens of websites copied the text without checking it.","t":"那家公司發布了一份關於新手機的新聞稿，而幾十個網站沒有查證就照抄了內容。"},{"w":"scoop","p":"n.","d":"an important story one newspaper reports first","c":"獨家新聞","s":"The student newspaper got a big scoop when it discovered the school's budget problems, and even national TV reported it later.","t":"學生報發現學校的預算問題時拿到了一則大獨家新聞，後來連全國電視台都報導了。"},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"only given to one news company","c":"獨家的","s":"The singer gave an exclusive interview to one magazine, so fans had to buy that magazine to read about her new album.","t":"那位歌手只接受一家雜誌的獨家專訪，所以粉絲必須買那本雜誌才能讀到她新專輯的消息。"},{"w":"byline","p":"n.","d":"the line that shows who wrote an article","c":"署名欄（作者署名）","s":"I was very proud to see my name in the byline of the school magazine, because it was my first published article.","t":"看到我的名字出現在校刊的署名欄上，我非常驕傲，因為那是我第一篇刊出的文章。"},{"w":"columnist","p":"n.","d":"a writer who regularly writes opinion pieces","c":"專欄作家","s":"The columnist writes about family life every Sunday, and many parents say her funny stories make them feel less alone.","t":"那位專欄作家每個星期日寫關於家庭生活的文章，許多父母說她有趣的故事讓他們覺得不那麼孤單。"},{"w":"op-ed","p":"n.","d":"an opinion article written by someone outside the newspaper","c":"特約評論；投書","s":"A doctor wrote an op-ed about the dangers of vaping, and the newspaper published it because many teenagers are affected.","t":"一位醫生寫了一篇關於電子菸危害的投書，報社刊登了它，因為許多青少年受到影響。"},{"w":"tabloid","p":"n.","d":"a popular newspaper with short, exciting stories about famous people","c":"小報；八卦報","s":"The tabloid printed a shocking story about the actor's private life, but later it had to admit that the story was false.","t":"那份小報刊登了一則關於那位演員私生活的驚人報導，但後來不得不承認那則報導是假的。"},{"w":"newsworthy","p":"adj.","d":"interesting or important enough to report","c":"有新聞價值的","s":"The editor said that a cat stuck in a tree was not newsworthy, but the story became popular online anyway.","t":"編輯說一隻卡在樹上的貓沒有新聞價值，但這則故事還是在網路上爆紅了。"},{"w":"breaking news","p":"n.phr.","d":"news about something that is happening right now","c":"即時新聞；快訊","s":"We were watching a cooking show when breaking news about the earthquake interrupted the programme, so everyone stopped and listened.","t":"我們正在看烹飪節目時，關於地震的即時新聞打斷了節目，所以大家都停下來聆聽。"},{"w":"investigative","p":"adj.","d":"trying to find hidden facts","c":"調查性的","s":"The investigative report took six months to complete, but it finally showed how the factory had been polluting the river.","t":"那篇調查報導花了六個月才完成，但最終揭露了工廠是如何汙染河流的。"},{"w":"whistle-blower","p":"n.","d":"a person who tells the public about wrongdoing at work","c":"吹哨者；揭弊者","s":"The whistle-blower lost her job after she reported the company's illegal dumping, but she said she did not regret telling the truth.","t":"那位吹哨者揭發公司非法傾倒廢棄物後丟了工作，但她說她不後悔說出真相。"},{"w":"informant","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives secret information to someone","c":"線人；消息提供者","s":"The journalist promised never to reveal the name of her informant, because he could lose his job if people found out.","t":"那名記者承諾絕不透露她線人的名字，因為如果別人發現，他可能會丟掉工作。"},{"w":"eyewitness","p":"n.","d":"a person who saw an event happen","c":"目擊者","s":"An eyewitness told reporters that the car was driving very fast, and her description helped the police understand the accident.","t":"一位目擊者告訴記者那輛車開得非常快，而她的描述幫助警方了解這起事故。"},{"w":"paparazzi","p":"n.","d":"photographers who follow famous people to take pictures","c":"狗仔隊","s":"The paparazzi waited outside the restaurant all evening, so the famous couple had to leave through the kitchen door.","t":"狗仔隊整晚守在餐廳外面，所以那對名人夫妻只好從廚房的門離開。"},{"w":"obituary","p":"n.","d":"a news article about a person who has recently died","c":"訃聞","s":"The local paper published an obituary for the old teacher, and many former students shared it online with kind memories.","t":"地方報紙為那位老教師刊登了一則訃聞，許多以前的學生在網路上分享並寫下溫馨的回憶。"},{"w":"news outlet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company or website that publishes news","c":"新聞媒體；新聞管道","s":"Several news outlet reported the same false story, because they all copied it from one social media post without checking.","t":"好幾家新聞媒體報導了同一則假新聞，因為它們都沒有查證就從一則社群貼文抄來。"},{"w":"press freedom","p":"n.phr.","d":"the right of the media to report without government control","c":"新聞自由","s":"Taiwan ranks highly for press freedom, so journalists here can criticise the government without fear of going to prison.","t":"台灣的新聞自由排名很高，所以這裡的記者可以批評政府而不必擔心坐牢。"},{"w":"paywall","p":"n.","d":"a system that makes you pay to read online articles","c":"付費牆","s":"I wanted to read the full article, but it was behind a paywall, so I only saw the first two paragraphs.","t":"我想讀完整篇文章，但它被放在付費牆後面，所以我只看到前兩段。"},{"w":"sensational","p":"adj.","d":"made to shock or excite people rather than inform them","c":"聳動的；譁眾取寵的","s":"The website uses sensational headlines to attract clicks, but the articles themselves usually contain very little real information.","t":"那個網站使用聳動的標題來吸引點擊，但文章本身通常只有很少的真實資訊。"},{"w":"censor","p":"v.","d":"to remove parts of news, books or films that authorities dislike","c":"審查；刪減","s":"The government censor the documentary before it was shown, so viewers never saw the scenes of the protest.","t":"政府在紀錄片播出前就審查刪剪了它，所以觀眾從未看到抗議的畫面。"},{"w":"censorship","p":"n.","d":"the control of what people can say, read or watch","c":"審查制度","s":"Strict censorship means that some citizens cannot use foreign websites, so they often rely on VPNs to read international news.","t":"嚴格的審查制度意味著有些公民無法使用外國網站，所以他們常依靠 VPN 來閱讀國際新聞。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Broadcasting & Traditional Media 廣播與傳統媒體","cards":[{"w":"broadcast","p":"v.","d":"to send out a programme on TV or radio","c":"播出；廣播","s":"The final match was broadcast live on national television, so millions of people watched it at home and in restaurants.","t":"那場決賽在全國電視台現場播出，所以數百萬人在家裡和餐廳收看。"},{"w":"broadcaster","p":"n.","d":"a company or person that makes TV or radio programmes","c":"廣播公司；播報員","s":"The public broadcaster does not show adverts, because it is paid for by taxes rather than by companies.","t":"那家公共廣播公司不播放廣告，因為它的經費來自稅收而不是企業。"},{"w":"television","p":"n.","d":"a system or machine for watching programmes","c":"電視","s":"Fewer young people watch television in the evening now, because they prefer short videos on their phones.","t":"現在晚上看電視的年輕人比較少了，因為他們比較喜歡在手機上看短影片。"},{"w":"programme","p":"n.","d":"a show on TV or radio","c":"節目","s":"My favourite programme is a science show for teenagers, and each episode explains one strange fact about nature.","t":"我最喜歡的節目是一個給青少年看的科學節目，每一集都解釋一個關於大自然的奇特事實。"},{"w":"documentary","p":"n.","d":"a film or programme that gives facts about a real topic","c":"紀錄片","s":"We watched a documentary about plastic in the ocean, and afterwards the whole class decided to stop using plastic straws.","t":"我們看了一部關於海洋塑膠的紀錄片，之後全班決定不再使用塑膠吸管。"},{"w":"talk show","p":"n.phr.","d":"a programme where a host chats with guests","c":"脫口秀；談話節目","s":"The actor appeared on a late-night talk show, and he told funny stories about the mistakes he made while filming.","t":"那位演員上了一個深夜談話節目，他講了一些拍片時犯錯的趣事。"},{"w":"sitcom","p":"n.","d":"a funny TV series about the same characters","c":"情境喜劇","s":"My parents love an old American sitcom about six friends in New York, so they watch the episodes again and again.","t":"我爸媽很喜歡一部關於紐約六個朋友的老美國情境喜劇，所以他們一再重看那些集數。"},{"w":"soap opera","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long-running drama series about people's lives","c":"肥皂劇；連續劇","s":"My grandmother never misses her favourite soap opera, and she gets very upset when the characters argue or fall in love.","t":"我奶奶從不錯過她最愛的連續劇，而且劇中人物吵架或談戀愛時她都會很激動。"},{"w":"reality show","p":"n.phr.","d":"a programme that films ordinary people in real situations","c":"真人實境秀","s":"The reality show claims to show real life, but some contestants later admitted that many scenes had been planned in advance.","t":"那個真人實境秀聲稱呈現真實生活，但有些參賽者後來承認許多場景是事先安排好的。"},{"w":"viewer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches TV or videos","c":"觀眾","s":"Many viewer complained about the violent scenes, so the channel moved the programme to a later time.","t":"許多觀眾抱怨那些暴力場面，所以電視台把節目移到較晚的時段。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch, read or listen to something","c":"觀眾；聽眾；受眾","s":"The speaker made a joke at the beginning, and the whole audience laughed, so she felt much more relaxed.","t":"講者在一開始開了個玩笑，全場聽眾都笑了，所以她感覺放鬆多了。"},{"w":"ratings","p":"n.","d":"numbers showing how many people watch a programme","c":"收視率","s":"The show's ratings fell sharply after the main actor left, so the network decided to cancel it.","t":"那位主角離開後，節目的收視率急劇下滑，所以電視網決定停播。"},{"w":"prime time","p":"n.phr.","d":"the evening hours when most people watch TV","c":"黃金時段","s":"Adverts shown during prime time are very expensive, because that is when the largest number of families are watching.","t":"在黃金時段播出的廣告非常昂貴，因為那時收看的家庭最多。"},{"w":"commercial break","p":"n.phr.","d":"a pause in a programme for adverts","c":"廣告時間；進廣告","s":"During the commercial break I quickly made some tea, but I missed the start of the next part of the film.","t":"廣告時間的時候我很快泡了杯茶，但我錯過了電影下一段的開頭。"},{"w":"host","p":"n.","d":"the person who introduces a show and talks to guests","c":"主持人","s":"The host of the quiz show was friendly and calm, so even nervous contestants were able to answer well.","t":"那個益智節目的主持人友善又沉穩，所以連緊張的參賽者都能回答得很好。"},{"w":"presenter","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces a TV or radio programme","c":"節目主持人；主播","s":"The weather presenter pointed to the map and warned that heavy rain would arrive by the weekend, so people prepared early.","t":"氣象主播指著地圖警告大雨將在週末前到來，所以民眾提早做好準備。"},{"w":"newsreader","p":"n.","d":"a person who reads the news on TV or radio","c":"新聞播報員；主播","s":"The newsreader stayed calm while she reported the disaster, but viewers could see that she was deeply affected.","t":"那位新聞主播報導災難時保持冷靜，但觀眾看得出她深受影響。"},{"w":"episode","p":"n.","d":"one part of a TV or radio series","c":"（一）集","s":"The last episode of the series ended with a big surprise, and fans have been discussing it online ever since.","t":"那部影集的最後一集以一個大驚喜收尾，粉絲們從那時起就一直在網路上討論。"},{"w":"studio","p":"n.","d":"a room where TV, radio or music is recorded","c":"攝影棚；錄音室","s":"We visited a TV studio on our school trip, and we were surprised by how small the set looked in real life.","t":"我們校外教學參觀了一間電視攝影棚，我們很驚訝實際上的布景看起來那麼小。"},{"w":"podcast","p":"n.","d":"a recorded audio programme you can download or stream","c":"播客；Podcast節目","s":"I listen to an English podcast on the bus every morning, and it has really improved my listening skills.","t":"我每天早上在公車上聽一個英文播客節目，它真的提升了我的聽力。"},{"w":"airwaves","p":"n.","d":"the radio signals used for broadcasting","c":"廣播電波；廣播節目","s":"The song was all over the airwaves that summer, so you could hear it in shops, taxis and almost every café.","t":"那年夏天那首歌充斥廣播電台，所以在商店、計程車和幾乎每家咖啡廳都聽得到。"},{"w":"newscast","p":"n.","d":"a news programme on TV or radio","c":"新聞報導節目","s":"My parents watch the evening newscast every day at seven, and they always discuss the main stories during dinner.","t":"晚間新聞節目是我爸媽每天七點必看的，晚餐時他們總是討論其中的主要新聞。"},{"w":"on-demand","p":"adj.","d":"available whenever you want it","c":"隨選的","s":"The on-demand service lets you watch shows whenever you like, so you no longer need to wait for a fixed time.","t":"這個隨選服務讓你隨時想看就看，所以你不再需要等固定的時段。"},{"w":"magazine","p":"n.","d":"a thin weekly or monthly publication with articles and pictures","c":"雜誌","s":"She bought a science magazine at the airport, and the article about space travel kept her busy during the long flight.","t":"她在機場買了一本科學雜誌，那篇關於太空旅行的文章讓她在漫長的航程中不無聊。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"one printed version of a newspaper, book or magazine","c":"版；版本；期","s":"The morning edition of the paper had already been printed, so the late news about the election appeared online first.","t":"報紙的早報版已經印好了，所以選舉的最新消息先出現在網路上。"},{"w":"print media","p":"n.phr.","d":"newspapers and magazines printed on paper","c":"平面媒體","s":"print media has lost many readers to the internet, but some people still trust printed newspapers more than websites.","t":"平面媒體已經因網路流失了許多讀者，但有些人仍然比較相信紙本報紙而不是網站。"},{"w":"mass media","p":"n.phr.","d":"TV, radio and newspapers that reach large numbers of people","c":"大眾傳播媒體","s":"The mass media can shape public opinion quickly, so it has a responsibility to report facts carefully.","t":"大眾傳媒能迅速塑造輿論，所以它有責任謹慎地報導事實。"},{"w":"subtitle","p":"n.","d":"words at the bottom of the screen translating speech","c":"字幕","s":"I watch Korean dramas with English subtitle, because it helps me learn new words while I enjoy the story.","t":"我看韓劇時開英文字幕，因為這能幫助我在享受劇情的同時學新單字。"},{"w":"listener","p":"n.","d":"a person who listens to a radio programme","c":"聽眾","s":"One listener called the radio station to share her story, and the host thanked her for being so honest.","t":"一位聽眾打電話到電台分享她的故事，主持人感謝她如此坦誠。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Social Media & the Internet 社群媒體與網路","cards":[{"w":"social media","p":"n.phr.","d":"websites and apps where people share content and talk","c":"社群媒體","s":"Most teenagers get their news from social media, but they do not always check whether the stories are true.","t":"大多數青少年從社群媒體獲得新聞，但他們不一定會查證那些報導是否屬實。"},{"w":"post","p":"v.","d":"to put a message or picture online","c":"發布；張貼（貼文）","s":"She post a photo of her lunch every day, and her friends always leave funny comments under it.","t":"她每天發布一張午餐照片，而她的朋友總是在下面留些好笑的留言。"},{"w":"repost","p":"v.","d":"to share someone else's post again","c":"轉發；轉貼","s":"Thousands of people repost the video of the lost dog, so its owner found it within a few hours.","t":"數千人轉發了那段走失狗狗的影片，所以牠的主人在幾小時內就找到了牠。"},{"w":"follower","p":"n.","d":"a person who chooses to see someone's posts","c":"追蹤者；粉絲","s":"The baker has over 50,000 follower online, so new customers visit his shop from all over the city.","t":"那位麵包師傅在網路上有超過五萬名追蹤者，所以全市各地都有新客人來他的店。"},{"w":"influencer","p":"n.","d":"a person with many online followers who affects what they buy","c":"網紅；意見領袖","s":"The influencer was paid to recommend the face cream, but she did not tell her followers that it was an advert.","t":"那位網紅拿錢推薦那款面霜，但她沒有告訴追蹤者那是廣告。"},{"w":"vlogger","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes video blogs","c":"影音部落客；Vlogger","s":"The travel vlogger films every meal and every hotel room, and his videos have made a small town in Taiwan famous.","t":"那位旅遊影音部落客拍下每一餐和每一間飯店房間，而他的影片讓台灣一個小鎮出了名。"},{"w":"blogger","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes an online journal","c":"部落客","s":"The food blogger gave the restaurant a bad review, so the owner invited her back to try the new menu.","t":"那位美食部落客給那家餐廳負評，所以老闆邀請她再來試試新菜單。"},{"w":"hashtag","p":"n.","d":"a word after the # sign used to group posts","c":"主題標籤；#標籤","s":"People used the same hashtag to share photos of the clean-up, so it was easy to see how many beaches had been cleared.","t":"人們用同一個主題標籤分享淨灘照片，所以很容易看出有多少海灘被清理乾淨了。"},{"w":"viral","p":"adj.","d":"spread very quickly to many people online","c":"爆紅的；病毒式傳播的","s":"A video of a cat playing the piano went viral overnight, and the owner was soon invited onto several TV shows.","t":"一段貓彈鋼琴的影片一夜之間爆紅，主人很快就被邀請上好幾個電視節目。"},{"w":"meme","p":"n.","d":"a funny image or text copied and shared online","c":"迷因；梗圖","s":"My brother sent me a meme about exams, and it was so true that I laughed while I was studying.","t":"我哥傳給我一張關於考試的梗圖，內容太真實了，害我讀書時笑出來。"},{"w":"emoji","p":"n.","d":"a small picture used in digital messages","c":"表情符號","s":"She replied with a smiling emoji, but I could not tell whether she was happy or just being polite.","t":"她回了一個微笑的表情符號，但我分辨不出她是開心還是只是出於禮貌。"},{"w":"selfie","p":"n.","d":"a photo you take of yourself","c":"自拍照","s":"Tourists were taking selfie at the edge of the cliff, so the park added a fence to keep them safe.","t":"遊客在懸崖邊拍自拍照，所以公園加裝了圍欄保障他們的安全。"},{"w":"profile","p":"n.","d":"the page with information about a user","c":"個人檔案；個人頁面","s":"Before the interview, the manager looked at my online profile, so I was glad that I had removed my old party photos.","t":"面試前經理看了我的網路個人頁面，所以我很慶幸自己已經刪掉了以前的派對照片。"},{"w":"notification","p":"n.","d":"a message on your phone telling you something new","c":"通知","s":"My phone kept showing notification during class, so I finally turned them off and concentrated much better.","t":"上課時我的手機一直跳出通知，所以我終於把它們關掉，結果專心多了。"},{"w":"livestream","p":"v.","d":"to show video on the internet as it happens","c":"直播","s":"The band livestream their concert for fans who could not buy tickets, and over a million people watched online.","t":"那個樂團為買不到票的粉絲直播了演唱會，超過一百萬人在線上觀看。"},{"w":"content creator","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who makes videos, posts or other online material","c":"內容創作者","s":"Being a content creator looks easy, but many spend hours filming and editing a video that lasts only one minute.","t":"當內容創作者看似簡單，但許多人要花好幾小時拍攝和剪輯一部只有一分鐘的影片。"},{"w":"troll","p":"n.","d":"a person who posts rude messages to upset others","c":"網路酸民","s":"A troll left nasty comments under every photo she posted, so she decided to block him and ignore his messages.","t":"一位酸民在她發的每張照片下留惡毒留言，所以她決定封鎖他並不理會他的訊息。"},{"w":"cyberbullying","p":"n.","d":"hurting or threatening someone online","c":"網路霸凌","s":"cyberbullying can follow students home from school, because hurtful messages arrive on their phones at any time.","t":"網路霸凌會讓學生回到家也逃不掉，因為傷人的訊息隨時都會傳到他們的手機上。"},{"w":"echo chamber","p":"n.phr.","d":"an online space where you only hear opinions like your own","c":"同溫層；回音室","s":"If you only follow people who agree with you, you may end up in an echo chamber, and you will never hear other views.","t":"如果你只追蹤和你意見相同的人，你可能會陷入同溫層，而且永遠聽不到其他觀點。"},{"w":"filter bubble","p":"n.phr.","d":"when apps only show you content they think you like","c":"過濾氣泡","s":"The app keeps showing me the same kind of videos, so I worry that I am stuck in a filter bubble.","t":"那個應用程式一直推給我同類型的影片，所以我擔心自己被困在過濾氣泡裡。"},{"w":"screenshot","p":"n.","d":"a picture of what is on a screen","c":"螢幕截圖","s":"He deleted the rude message quickly, but someone had already taken a screenshot, so everyone saw what he had written.","t":"他很快就刪掉了那則無禮的訊息，但有人已經截圖了，所以大家都看到他寫了什麼。"},{"w":"username","p":"n.","d":"the name you use to log in to a website or app","c":"使用者名稱；帳號名稱","s":"I forgot my username for the game, so I had to use my email address to get into my account.","t":"我忘了那款遊戲的使用者名稱，所以必須用電子郵件地址才能登入帳號。"},{"w":"search engine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a website that helps you find information online","c":"搜尋引擎","s":"I typed the question into a search engine, but the first results were all adverts, so I scrolled down for better sources.","t":"我把問題輸入搜尋引擎，但前幾個結果都是廣告，所以我往下滑找更好的資料來源。"},{"w":"website","p":"n.","d":"a set of pages on the internet","c":"網站","s":"The website looked professional, but it had no contact details, so my teacher said we should not trust it.","t":"那個網站看起來很專業，但沒有任何聯絡資訊，所以老師說我們不應該相信它。"},{"w":"direct message","p":"n.phr.","d":"a private message sent on social media","c":"私訊","s":"She sent me a direct message instead of commenting publicly, because she did not want everyone to read it.","t":"她傳私訊給我而不是公開留言，因為她不想讓大家都讀到。"},{"w":"group chat","p":"n.phr.","d":"an online conversation with several people at once","c":"群組聊天","s":"Our class group chat gets hundreds of messages every night, so I mute it while I am doing homework.","t":"我們班的群組聊天每晚都有上百則訊息，所以我寫作業時會把它設為靜音。"},{"w":"unfollow","p":"v.","d":"to stop seeing someone's posts on social media","c":"取消追蹤","s":"I unfollow that account because it kept posting angry and false stories, and now my feed feels much calmer.","t":"我取消追蹤了那個帳號，因為它一直發布憤怒和不實的報導，現在我的動態感覺平靜多了。"},{"w":"block","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from contacting you online","c":"封鎖","s":"If a stranger sends you unkind messages, you should block the account and tell an adult you trust.","t":"如果陌生人傳給你不友善的訊息，你應該封鎖那個帳號，並告訴你信任的大人。"},{"w":"anonymity","p":"n.","d":"the state of hiding your real name","c":"匿名（性）","s":"anonymity makes some people braver online, but it also allows others to say cruel things without any consequences.","t":"匿名性讓有些人在網路上更敢說話，但也讓另一些人說出殘忍的話而不必承擔後果。"},{"w":"doomscrolling","p":"n.","d":"reading bad news online for too long","c":"末日滾動；狂刷負面新聞","s":"After an hour of doomscrolling before bed, I felt anxious and could not sleep, so I now leave my phone in the kitchen.","t":"睡前狂刷負面新聞一小時後，我感到焦慮又睡不著，所以我現在都把手機放在廚房。"},{"w":"screen time","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time you spend looking at a screen","c":"螢幕使用時間","s":"My parents limit my screen time to two hours a day, so I have more time for sport and reading.","t":"我爸媽把我的螢幕使用時間限制在一天兩小時，所以我有更多時間運動和閱讀。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Misinformation & Fake News 假訊息與假新聞","cards":[{"w":"disinformation","p":"n.","d":"false information spread on purpose to trick people","c":"蓄意造假的訊息；假訊息","s":"The disinformation campaign used fake accounts to spread lies about the vaccine, so many parents became afraid to protect their children.","t":"那場假訊息攻勢利用假帳號散播關於疫苗的謊言，所以許多家長變得不敢讓孩子接種。"},{"w":"fake news","p":"n.phr.","d":"false stories that look like real news","c":"假新聞","s":"My uncle shared a story about free money from the government, but it was fake news, so I showed him the official website.","t":"我叔叔分享了一則政府發放免費現金的消息，但那是假新聞，所以我給他看了官方網站。"},{"w":"hoax","p":"n.","d":"a trick that makes people believe something false","c":"騙局；惡作劇","s":"The photo of a shark swimming on the highway was a hoax, but thousands of people believed it during the flood.","t":"那張鯊魚在高速公路上游泳的照片是個惡作劇，但淹水期間成千上萬的人都信以為真。"},{"w":"rumour","p":"n.","d":"a story passed between people that may not be true","c":"謠言；傳聞","s":"A rumour spread that the school would close for a week, but the principal soon announced that it was not true.","t":"有謠言說學校會停課一週，但校長很快就宣布那不是真的。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"n.","d":"talk about other people's private lives","c":"八卦；閒話","s":"The office gossip about the manager turned out to be false, but it had already damaged her reputation.","t":"辦公室裡關於經理的八卦結果是假的，但它已經損害了她的名聲。"},{"w":"propaganda","p":"n.","d":"information used by a government or group to control opinions","c":"政治宣傳","s":"During the war, both sides used propaganda posters to make their own soldiers look like heroes and the enemy look evil.","t":"戰爭期間雙方都用宣傳海報把自己的士兵塑造成英雄，把敵人塑造成邪惡的。"},{"w":"conspiracy theory","p":"n.phr.","d":"a belief that a secret group caused an event","c":"陰謀論","s":"He believes a conspiracy theory that the moon landing was filmed in a studio, although scientists have shown clear evidence against it.","t":"他相信登月是在攝影棚拍攝的陰謀論，儘管科學家已提出明確的反駁證據。"},{"w":"clickbait","p":"n.","d":"online content with a misleading title to get clicks","c":"釣魚標題；點擊誘餌","s":"The title promised a shocking secret about celebrities, but it was just clickbait, and the article said nothing new.","t":"那個標題承諾要揭露名人驚人的秘密，但它只是釣魚標題，文章沒有任何新內容。"},{"w":"falsehood","p":"n.","d":"a statement that is not true","c":"謊言；不實之詞","s":"The politician repeated the same falsehood in every speech, so many voters began to believe it was true.","t":"那位政治人物在每場演講中重複同一個不實說法，所以許多選民開始相信那是真的。"},{"w":"half-truth","p":"n.","d":"a statement that is partly true but hides important facts","c":"半真半假的話","s":"The advert said the drink had \"no added sugar\", which was a half-truth, because the juice itself was full of natural sugar.","t":"那則廣告說這飲料「無添加糖」，這是半真半假的說法，因為果汁本身就充滿天然糖分。"},{"w":"misquote","p":"v.","d":"to repeat someone's words wrongly","c":"錯誤引用（某人的話）","s":"The singer said the newspaper had misquote her, because she never said that she hated her fans.","t":"那位歌手說報紙錯誤引用了她的話，因為她從未說過她討厭她的粉絲。"},{"w":"doctored","p":"adj.","d":"changed in a dishonest way","c":"竄改過的；動過手腳的","s":"The doctored photo made the crowd look much bigger, but experts noticed that some faces appeared twice.","t":"那張動過手腳的照片讓人群看起來大很多，但專家注意到有些臉出現了兩次。"},{"w":"smear campaign","p":"n.phr.","d":"an organised effort to damage someone's reputation with lies","c":"抹黑行動","s":"The candidate said she was the victim of a smear campaign, because fake stories about her family appeared just before the election.","t":"那位候選人說她是抹黑行動的受害者，因為選舉前夕突然出現許多關於她家人的假消息。"},{"w":"defamation","p":"n.","d":"harming someone's reputation by saying false things","c":"誹謗","s":"The restaurant owner sued the blogger for defamation, because the review falsely claimed that customers had become ill.","t":"餐廳老闆控告那位部落客誹謗，因為那篇評論不實地聲稱顧客吃了生病。"},{"w":"libel","p":"n.","d":"false written statements that damage someone's reputation","c":"（書面）誹謗","s":"The magazine had to pay a large fine for libel, because it published false claims about a businessman.","t":"那本雜誌因書面誹謗必須支付一大筆罰款，因為它刊登了關於一位商人的不實指控。"},{"w":"slander","p":"n.","d":"false spoken statements that damage someone's reputation","c":"（口頭）誹謗；中傷","s":"What he said about his neighbour on the radio was slander, so the neighbour asked a lawyer for help.","t":"他在廣播上說他鄰居的那些話是中傷，所以那位鄰居請律師幫忙。"},{"w":"spin","p":"n.","d":"presenting information in a way that makes you look good","c":"（對消息的）粉飾；操弄說法","s":"The company called the job cuts \"a new start\", but everyone knew it was just spin, and the workers were still angry.","t":"公司把裁員稱為「新的開始」，但大家都知道那只是粉飾說法，員工們仍然很憤怒。"},{"w":"spin doctor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person paid to make news look good for a politician","c":"公關操盤手；政治化妝師","s":"The minister's spin doctor quickly changed the story, so the scandal disappeared from the news within two days.","t":"部長的公關操盤手很快就轉移了焦點，所以那件醜聞兩天內就從新聞中消失了。"},{"w":"bot","p":"n.","d":"a computer program that acts like a real user online","c":"機器人帳號；網軍程式","s":"Many of the accounts praising the product were bot, because they all posted the same message at the same time.","t":"許多稱讚那項產品的帳號都是機器人帳號，因為它們都在同一時間發布同樣的訊息。"},{"w":"troll farm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group paid to post false or angry comments online","c":"網軍工廠","s":"Investigators found that a troll farm had created thousands of fake profiles, and they were all spreading the same rumours.","t":"調查人員發現一個網軍工廠創造了數千個假帳號，而它們都在散播同樣的謠言。"},{"w":"fearmongering","p":"n.","d":"spreading fear to make people believe or do something","c":"散播恐懼；危言聳聽","s":"Some news channels were accused of fearmongering during the outbreak, because they showed panic but gave little useful advice.","t":"疫情期間有些新聞台被指控散播恐慌，因為它們只呈現恐慌卻很少提供有用的建議。"},{"w":"hearsay","p":"n.","d":"information you heard from others but cannot prove","c":"傳聞；道聽塗說","s":"The report was based on hearsay rather than real evidence, so the editor refused to publish it.","t":"那篇報導是根據道聽塗說而不是真正的證據，所以編輯拒絕刊登它。"},{"w":"unverified","p":"adj.","d":"not yet checked or proved to be true","c":"未經證實的","s":"The TV channel showed unverified videos from the scene, but later some of them turned out to be from a different country.","t":"那家電視台播出了現場未經證實的影片，但後來其中一些被證實來自別的國家。"},{"w":"gullible","p":"adj.","d":"too easily tricked into believing things","c":"容易受騙的","s":"My little brother is so gullible that he believed a website saying cats can speak French, and he tried to teach ours.","t":"我弟弟非常容易受騙，他相信了一個說貓會講法語的網站，還試著教我們家的貓。"},{"w":"impostor","p":"n.","d":"a person who pretends to be someone else","c":"冒牌貨；冒名者","s":"An impostor created an account with the actor's photos, so fans sent money to someone who was not really him.","t":"一個冒名者用那位演員的照片開了帳號，所以粉絲把錢匯給了一個根本不是他的人。"},{"w":"satire","p":"n.","d":"humour that makes fun of people or ideas to criticise them","c":"諷刺作品","s":"The article was satire from a comedy website, but some readers did not understand the joke and believed it was real news.","t":"那篇文章是喜劇網站的諷刺作品，但有些讀者不懂那是玩笑，以為是真的新聞。"},{"w":"parody","p":"n.","d":"a funny copy of something that exaggerates it","c":"模仿惡搞作品","s":"The students made a parody of the school's promotional video, and even the teachers laughed when they watched it.","t":"學生們拍了一部學校宣傳影片的惡搞版，連老師們看了都笑了。"},{"w":"cherry-pick","p":"v.","d":"to choose only facts that support your view","c":"挑選對自己有利的（事實）","s":"The report cherry-pick the best results from the study, so it ignored the data showing that the drug did not work for most people.","t":"那份報告只挑選研究中最好的結果，所以它忽略了顯示這藥物對多數人無效的數據。"},{"w":"partisan","p":"adj.","d":"strongly supporting one political party","c":"偏袒某一黨派的","s":"The TV station is very partisan, so it rarely reports any good news about the opposition party.","t":"那家電視台非常偏袒特定政黨，所以它很少報導任何關於反對黨的好消息。"},{"w":"infodemic","p":"n.","d":"too much information, including false information, during a crisis","c":"資訊疫情；訊息氾濫","s":"During the pandemic there was an infodemic of advice online, and it was hard to know which tips were safe.","t":"疫情期間網路上出現了建議的資訊疫情，很難知道哪些建議是安全的。"},{"w":"outrage","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of anger and shock","c":"憤慨；義憤","s":"The video caused outrage online, but later people discovered that it had been edited to look much worse.","t":"那段影片在網路上引起公憤，但後來人們發現它被剪輯得看起來更嚴重。"},{"w":"inflammatory","p":"adj.","d":"likely to make people angry or violent","c":"煽動性的；激起憤怒的","s":"The post used inflammatory language about immigrants, so the platform removed it and suspended the account.","t":"那則貼文使用了關於移民的煽動性語言，所以平台刪除了它並停用該帳號。"},{"w":"sensationalism","p":"n.","d":"presenting news in a shocking way to attract attention","c":"譁眾取寵的報導手法；煽情主義","s":"sensationalism helps sell newspapers, but it often makes small risks seem much bigger than they really are.","t":"煽情主義有助於賣報紙，但它常把小風險渲染得比實際嚴重得多。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Fact-Checking & Media Literacy 事實查核與媒體素養","cards":[{"w":"fact-check","p":"v.","d":"to make sure that information is correct","c":"查核事實","s":"Before you share a shocking story, you should fact-check it on a reliable website, because many viral posts are false.","t":"在分享一則驚人的消息之前，你應該到可靠的網站查核事實，因為許多爆紅的貼文是假的。"},{"w":"fact-checker","p":"n.","d":"a person or group that checks if claims are true","c":"事實查核員；查核機構","s":"A fact-checker found that the quote was invented, so the newspaper removed the article and apologised.","t":"一位事實查核員發現那句引言是捏造的，所以報社撤下文章並道歉。"},{"w":"media literacy","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ability to judge and understand news and media","c":"媒體素養","s":"Our school teaches media literacy in Year 10, so students learn how to recognise fake photos and misleading headlines.","t":"我們學校在十年級教媒體素養，所以學生學習如何辨認假照片和誤導性標題。"},{"w":"reverse image search","p":"n.phr.","d":"a search that finds where a picture first appeared","c":"以圖搜圖；反向圖片搜尋","s":"I did a reverse image search on the photo, and I found that it was taken five years earlier in another country.","t":"我對那張照片做了以圖搜圖，發現它是五年前在另一個國家拍的。"},{"w":"citation","p":"n.","d":"a note showing where information came from","c":"引用；出處","s":"Wikipedia asks writers to add a citation for every fact, so readers can check the original source themselves.","t":"維基百科要求作者為每個事實加上出處，讓讀者可以自己查證原始來源。"},{"w":"cross-check","p":"v.","d":"to check information using a different source","c":"交叉比對；交叉核對","s":"Good reporters cross-check every claim with at least two sources, because one person might be mistaken or lying.","t":"優秀的記者會用至少兩個來源交叉核對每一項說法，因為一個人可能弄錯或說謊。"},{"w":"retraction","p":"n.","d":"a statement saying something published earlier was wrong","c":"撤回聲明；撤稿","s":"The magazine printed a retraction the following week, but far fewer people saw it than the original false story.","t":"那本雜誌隔週刊登了撤回聲明，但看到的人比原本那則假報導少得多。"},{"w":"correction","p":"n.","d":"a notice that fixes a mistake in a report","c":"更正啟事；更正","s":"The website added a correction at the bottom of the article, because the date of the event had been wrong.","t":"那個網站在文章底部加上了更正啟事，因為活動日期寫錯了。"},{"w":"disclaimer","p":"n.","d":"a statement saying you are not responsible for something","c":"免責聲明","s":"The video had a disclaimer saying it was for entertainment only, but many viewers still treated it as medical advice.","t":"那部影片有一則免責聲明說它僅供娛樂，但許多觀眾仍然把它當作醫療建議。"},{"w":"reputable","p":"adj.","d":"known to be honest and reliable","c":"聲譽良好的；可信賴的","s":"For your project, please use reputable sources such as university websites, because blogs may contain personal opinions.","t":"做專題時請使用信譽良好的資料來源，例如大學網站，因為部落格可能包含個人意見。"},{"w":"authoritative","p":"adj.","d":"trusted because it comes from an expert","c":"權威的；可信的","s":"The health ministry's website is the most authoritative source of vaccine information, so I always check it first.","t":"衛福部的網站是疫苗資訊最權威的來源，所以我總是先查看它。"},{"w":"lateral reading","p":"n.phr.","d":"checking a site by reading what other sites say about it","c":"橫向閱讀","s":"Instead of staying on one website, try lateral reading, because other sources can tell you whether that site is trustworthy.","t":"不要只停留在一個網站上，試試橫向閱讀，因為其他來源可以告訴你那個網站是否可信。"},{"w":"timestamp","p":"n.","d":"the date and time when something was posted or recorded","c":"時間戳記","s":"The timestamp on the video showed it was filmed in 2019, so it could not be from yesterday's storm.","t":"影片上的時間戳記顯示它是在 2019 年拍的，所以它不可能是昨天暴風雨的畫面。"},{"w":"metadata","p":"n.","d":"hidden information about a digital file","c":"詮釋資料；後設資料","s":"Experts studied the photo's metadata, and they discovered the exact phone and date used to take it.","t":"專家研究了照片的詮釋資料，發現了拍攝時所用的手機型號與確切日期。"},{"w":"watermark","p":"n.","d":"a faint logo on an image to show who owns it","c":"浮水印","s":"The photographer adds a watermark to every picture, so other websites cannot use her work without permission.","t":"那位攝影師在每張照片上都加浮水印，所以其他網站無法未經許可使用她的作品。"},{"w":"evidence-based","p":"adj.","d":"based on facts from research","c":"以證據為基礎的；實證的","s":"The doctor only gives evidence-based advice, so she told us not to trust diet tips from random videos.","t":"那位醫生只給有實證根據的建議，所以她告訴我們不要相信隨便哪部影片裡的減肥秘訣。"},{"w":"moderator","p":"n.","d":"a person who checks and controls posts in an online group","c":"版主；內容審核員","s":"The forum moderator deletes rude comments quickly, so the discussion usually stays friendly and helpful.","t":"那個論壇的版主很快就會刪除無禮的留言，所以討論通常保持友善且有幫助。"},{"w":"flag","p":"v.","d":"to mark something as possibly wrong or harmful","c":"標記；檢舉","s":"Users can flag posts that look false, and then the platform sends them to fact-checkers for review.","t":"使用者可以標記看起來不實的貼文，然後平台會把它們送交事實查核員審查。"},{"w":"takedown","p":"n.","d":"the removal of content from a website","c":"下架；移除","s":"After the singer complained, the website received a takedown notice, so the stolen song was removed within hours.","t":"那位歌手投訴後，網站收到了下架通知，所以被盜用的歌曲在幾小時內就被移除了。"},{"w":"mistrust","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that you cannot believe someone","c":"不信任；猜疑","s":"Years of false promises have created deep mistrust of politicians, so many young people no longer bother to vote.","t":"多年來的虛假承諾造成了對政治人物深深的不信任，所以許多年輕人不再費心去投票。"},{"w":"trust","p":"n.","d":"the belief that someone is honest and reliable","c":"信任","s":"Once a news channel loses viewers' trust, it is very difficult to win back, even if it apologises.","t":"一家新聞台一旦失去觀眾的信任，即使道歉也很難再贏回來。"},{"w":"slant","p":"n.","d":"a way of presenting news that favours one side","c":"偏頗角度；傾向","s":"The article had a clear political slant, because it quoted only people who supported the new law.","t":"那篇文章有明顯的政治傾向，因為它只引用了支持新法的人的話。"},{"w":"loaded language","p":"n.phr.","d":"words chosen to create strong emotions","c":"情緒性字眼；煽情用語","s":"The report used loaded language like \"invasion\" and \"disaster\", so readers felt scared before they knew the facts.","t":"那篇報導使用了「入侵」和「災難」等情緒性字眼，所以讀者在了解事實之前就感到害怕。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Advertising, PR & Persuasion 廣告、公關與說服","cards":[{"w":"advertising","p":"n.","d":"the business of telling people about products to sell them","c":"廣告業；廣告宣傳","s":"The company spends more money on advertising than on research, so its products are famous but not very good.","t":"那家公司花在廣告上的錢比研究還多，所以它的產品很有名但不太好。"},{"w":"advertisement","p":"n.","d":"a notice or video that tries to sell something","c":"廣告","s":"I saw an advertisement for a cheap phone online, but the price was much higher when I got to the shop.","t":"我在網路上看到一則便宜手機的廣告，但我到店裡時價格高得多。"},{"w":"advertiser","p":"n.","d":"a company that pays for adverts","c":"廣告主；廣告商","s":"Many advertiser left the platform after hateful posts appeared next to their adverts, so the company lost millions.","t":"仇恨貼文出現在廣告旁邊後，許多廣告主離開了那個平台，所以那家公司損失了數百萬。"},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short, catchy phrase used in advertising","c":"標語；口號","s":"The shop's slogan is \"Fresh every morning\", and customers remember it because it is short and easy to say.","t":"那家店的標語是「每天早上都新鮮」，顧客記得它，因為它又短又好念。"},{"w":"billboard","p":"n.","d":"a very large outdoor sign for adverts","c":"廣告看板","s":"A huge billboard beside the highway shows a new car, so thousands of drivers see it every day on their way to work.","t":"高速公路旁一面巨大的廣告看板展示一款新車，所以每天有數千名駕駛在上班途中看到它。"},{"w":"brochure","p":"n.","d":"a small magazine with pictures and information about a product or place","c":"小冊子；宣傳手冊","s":"The hotel brochure showed a quiet beach, but when we arrived the beach was crowded and full of rubbish.","t":"飯店的宣傳手冊展示了一片寧靜的海灘，但我們抵達時海灘擁擠又滿是垃圾。"},{"w":"flyer","p":"n.","d":"a printed paper giving information about an event or offer","c":"傳單","s":"A student handed me a flyer about the charity concert, and I decided to go because the tickets were cheap.","t":"一位學生遞給我一張慈善音樂會的傳單，我決定去，因為門票很便宜。"},{"w":"poster","p":"n.","d":"a large printed picture or notice on a wall","c":"海報","s":"We put up a poster about the beach clean-up in the school hall, and more than fifty students signed up.","t":"我們在學校大廳貼了一張淨灘活動的海報，有五十多位學生報名。"},{"w":"jingle","p":"n.","d":"a short, catchy song used in an advert","c":"廣告歌","s":"The jingle for the noodle advert was so catchy that my little sister sang it all day long.","t":"那則泡麵廣告的廣告歌太洗腦了，我妹妹一整天都在唱。"},{"w":"logo","p":"n.","d":"a symbol that represents a company","c":"商標；標誌","s":"The company changed its logo to a simpler design, but many customers preferred the old one and complained online.","t":"那家公司把標誌換成更簡單的設計，但許多顧客比較喜歡舊的，還在網路上抱怨。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a product name made by a particular company","c":"品牌","s":"My mother always buys the same brand of soap, because she trusts it and does not want to try new ones.","t":"我媽媽總是買同一個品牌的肥皂，因為她信任它，不想嘗試新的。"},{"w":"publicity","p":"n.","d":"attention given to someone or something by the media","c":"宣傳；曝光度","s":"The film got a lot of free publicity when its star was seen at the festival, so ticket sales rose quickly.","t":"那部電影的主角在影展亮相後，它獲得了大量免費曝光，所以票房迅速上升。"},{"w":"public relations","p":"n.phr.","d":"the work of creating a good image for an organisation","c":"公共關係；公關","s":"After the food poisoning case, the restaurant hired a public relations firm, because it needed to win back customers' trust.","t":"發生食物中毒事件後，那家餐廳聘請了一家公關公司，因為它需要贏回顧客的信任。"},{"w":"spokesperson","p":"n.","d":"a person who speaks officially for a group","c":"發言人","s":"A spokesperson for the airline apologised for the delays, but she did not explain why so many flights were cancelled.","t":"航空公司的發言人為延誤道歉，但她沒有解釋為什麼取消了那麼多班機。"},{"w":"marketing","p":"n.","d":"the work of promoting and selling products","c":"行銷","s":"The new drink was not very tasty, but clever marketing on social media made it popular with teenagers.","t":"那款新飲料不太好喝，但社群媒體上聰明的行銷讓它在青少年之間很受歡迎。"},{"w":"product placement","p":"n.phr.","d":"showing a brand inside a film or show to advertise it","c":"置入性行銷","s":"The hero drinks the same brand of coffee in every scene, so it is obvious that this is product placement.","t":"主角在每一幕都喝同一個牌子的咖啡，所以很明顯這是置入性行銷。"},{"w":"pop-up ad","p":"n.phr.","d":"an advert that suddenly appears in a new window online","c":"彈出式廣告","s":"A pop-up ad appeared while I was reading the news, and it was so hard to close that I left the website.","t":"我在看新聞時跳出一則彈出式廣告，它難關到我乾脆離開了那個網站。"},{"w":"sponsored content","p":"n.phr.","d":"material paid for by a company but made to look like normal posts","c":"業配內容；贊助內容","s":"Many travel videos are actually sponsored content, so the hotels in them may have paid for the good reviews.","t":"許多旅遊影片其實是業配內容，所以影片中的飯店可能付了錢換取好評。"},{"w":"catchphrase","p":"n.","d":"a short phrase that a famous person often says","c":"口頭禪；流行語","s":"The comedian's catchphrase became so popular that students repeated it in class, and some teachers found it annoying.","t":"那位喜劇演員的口頭禪變得非常流行，學生們在課堂上一直重複，有些老師覺得很煩。"},{"w":"testimonial","p":"n.","d":"a statement from a customer praising a product","c":"使用者推薦；見證","s":"The website was full of glowing testimonial, but I later learned that some of them were written by the company's staff.","t":"那個網站滿是讚不絕口的顧客推薦，但我後來得知其中一些是公司員工寫的。"},{"w":"mascot","p":"n.","d":"a character or animal that represents a team or company","c":"吉祥物","s":"The city's bear mascot appears at every festival, and children love taking pictures with it.","t":"這座城市的熊吉祥物出現在每個節慶活動上，孩子們很喜歡和它拍照。"},{"w":"rebrand","p":"v.","d":"to change the name or image of a company or product","c":"品牌重塑；改頭換面","s":"The airline rebrand itself after a terrible accident, because many passengers connected the old name with danger.","t":"那家航空公司在一場嚴重事故後進行了品牌重塑，因為許多乘客把舊名稱和危險聯想在一起。"},{"w":"consumer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or services","c":"消費者","s":"Every consumer has the right to know what is in their food, so the law requires clear labels on packaging.","t":"每位消費者都有權知道食物裡有什麼，所以法律要求包裝上有清楚的標示。"},{"w":"hype","p":"n.","d":"exaggerated excitement and advertising about something","c":"炒作；大肆宣傳","s":"There was so much hype about the new game, but when it was released it was full of bugs and many players were disappointed.","t":"那款新遊戲被大肆炒作，但發售時卻充滿錯誤，許多玩家都很失望。"},{"w":"buzz","p":"n.","d":"excited talk about something new","c":"話題；熱烈討論","s":"The trailer created a lot of buzz online, so the cinema added extra showings on the first weekend.","t":"那支預告片在網路上引起大量話題，所以電影院在首映週末加開了場次。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Communication & Interpersonal Skills 溝通與人際技巧","cards":[{"w":"interpersonal","p":"adj.","d":"relating to relationships between people","c":"人際的","s":"Good interpersonal skills are important for nurses, because they need to comfort worried patients and work closely with doctors.","t":"良好的人際技巧對護理師很重要，因為他們需要安撫擔心的病人並與醫生密切合作。"},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"using spoken words","c":"口頭的；言語的","s":"The coach gave us verbal instructions during the game, but the crowd was so loud that we could hardly hear him.","t":"教練在比賽中給了我們口頭指示，但觀眾太吵了，我們幾乎聽不到他說話。"},{"w":"non-verbal","p":"adj.","d":"without words, such as through body movements","c":"非語言的","s":"Smiling and nodding are non-verbal signals, and they show the speaker that you are listening carefully.","t":"微笑和點頭是非語言訊號，它們向說話者表示你正在仔細聆聽。"},{"w":"gesture","p":"n.","d":"a movement of the hand or head to show meaning","c":"手勢；姿態","s":"A thumbs-up is a friendly gesture in Taiwan, but in some countries it can be rude, so travellers should be careful.","t":"豎起大拇指在台灣是友善的手勢，但在某些國家可能是無禮的，所以旅客應該小心。"},{"w":"eye contact","p":"n.phr.","d":"looking directly into someone's eyes","c":"眼神接觸","s":"Try to make eye contact with the interviewer, because looking at the floor may make you seem nervous or dishonest.","t":"試著和面試官保持眼神接觸，因為看著地板可能會讓你顯得緊張或不誠實。"},{"w":"tone of voice","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way your voice sounds, showing your feelings","c":"語氣；說話的口氣","s":"She said \"fine\", but her tone of voice was cold, so I knew she was still angry with me.","t":"她說「好啊」，但她的語氣很冷淡，所以我知道她還在生我的氣。"},{"w":"active listening","p":"n.phr.","d":"listening carefully and showing that you understand","c":"主動聆聽；積極傾聽","s":"active listening means asking questions and repeating key points, so the other person feels that you really care.","t":"主動聆聽的意思是提出問題並複述重點，讓對方覺得你真的在乎。"},{"w":"small talk","p":"n.phr.","d":"polite conversation about unimportant things","c":"閒聊；寒暄","s":"At the party I made small talk about the weather, because I did not know anyone and felt a little shy.","t":"在派對上我聊了些天氣之類的閒聊，因為我誰都不認識，覺得有點害羞。"},{"w":"conversation","p":"n.","d":"a talk between two or more people","c":"對話；談話","s":"We had a long conversation about our future plans, and I realised that my best friend wants to study abroad.","t":"我們針對未來計畫進行了一段很長的談話，我才發現我最好的朋友想出國留學。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a discussion between groups to solve a problem","c":"對話；交流","s":"The two countries began a dialogue about the fishing dispute, so many people hoped the conflict would end peacefully.","t":"兩國就漁業爭端展開對話，所以許多人希望衝突能和平結束。"},{"w":"miscommunication","p":"n.","d":"a failure to share information clearly","c":"溝通不良；誤傳","s":"Because of a miscommunication between the teachers, two classes arrived at the gym at the same time, and nobody knew which one should leave.","t":"由於老師之間的溝通不良，兩個班同時到了體育館，沒有人知道哪一班該離開。"},{"w":"text message","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short written message sent by phone","c":"簡訊；手機訊息","s":"I sent my mother a text message to say the bus was late, so she would not worry when I got home after dark.","t":"我傳了一則簡訊給媽媽說公車誤點，這樣我天黑才到家時她就不會擔心。"},{"w":"voicemail","p":"n.","d":"a spoken message left on a phone","c":"語音留言","s":"The doctor did not answer, so I left a voicemail asking her to call me back when she was free.","t":"醫生沒有接電話，所以我留了一則語音留言，請她有空時回電給我。"},{"w":"email","p":"n.","d":"a message sent over the internet","c":"電子郵件","s":"I wrote a polite email to my teacher to ask for more time, and she kindly agreed to give me two extra days.","t":"我寫了一封有禮貌的電子郵件給老師要求延期，她很親切地同意多給我兩天。"},{"w":"pen pal","p":"n.phr.","d":"a friend in another place you write letters to","c":"筆友","s":"I have a pen pal in Canada, and we have been writing to each other for three years, so my English has improved a lot.","t":"我在加拿大有一位筆友，我們已經互相寫信三年了，所以我的英文進步很多。"},{"w":"video call","p":"n.phr.","d":"a call where people can see each other on screen","c":"視訊通話","s":"My grandparents live in the countryside, but we make a video call every Sunday, so they can see how the children are growing.","t":"我的祖父母住在鄉下，但我們每個星期天都會視訊通話，讓他們看看孩子們長大了多少。"},{"w":"public speaking","p":"n.phr.","d":"speaking in front of a large group of people","c":"公開演說","s":"Many students are afraid of public speaking, but practising in front of a mirror can help them feel more confident.","t":"許多學生害怕公開演說，但在鏡子前練習能幫助他們更有自信。"},{"w":"speech","p":"n.","d":"a formal talk given to an audience","c":"演講；致詞","s":"The principal gave a short speech at graduation, and several parents cried when she thanked the students' families.","t":"校長在畢業典禮上發表了簡短的致詞，她感謝學生家庭時，好幾位家長都哭了。"},{"w":"stage fright","p":"n.phr.","d":"nervousness before performing or speaking in public","c":"怯場","s":"He had terrible stage fright before the debate, but after the first minute he relaxed and spoke clearly.","t":"辯論前他嚴重怯場，但第一分鐘過後他就放鬆下來，說得很清楚。"},{"w":"etiquette","p":"n.","d":"the rules of polite behaviour","c":"禮節；禮儀","s":"Business etiquette is different in every country, so it is a good idea to learn the basics before you travel for work.","t":"商務禮儀在每個國家都不同，所以出差前先學一些基本知識是個好主意。"},{"w":"netiquette","p":"n.","d":"rules for polite behaviour on the internet","c":"網路禮儀","s":"Typing in capital letters is bad netiquette, because readers feel as if you are shouting at them.","t":"全用大寫字母打字是不好的網路禮儀，因為讀者會覺得你好像在對他們大吼。"},{"w":"courteous","p":"adj.","d":"polite and respectful","c":"有禮貌的；謙恭的","s":"The hotel staff were very courteous, so we felt welcome even though our room was not ready yet.","t":"飯店員工非常有禮貌，所以即使我們的房間還沒準備好，我們仍覺得受到歡迎。"},{"w":"tactful","p":"adj.","d":"careful not to upset people when saying difficult things","c":"圓融的；得體的","s":"She was tactful when she told me my essay needed work, so I did not feel hurt and was happy to improve it.","t":"她告訴我作文需要修改時說得很委婉得體，所以我沒有受傷，也很樂意改進。"},{"w":"blunt","p":"adj.","d":"saying exactly what you think, even if it is rude","c":"直率的；說話不客氣的","s":"My uncle is very blunt and says whatever he thinks, so he sometimes upsets people without meaning to.","t":"我叔叔說話非常直白，想到什麼就說什麼，所以他有時候會無意間讓人不高興。"},{"w":"talkative","p":"adj.","d":"liking to talk a lot","c":"健談的；愛說話的","s":"My little sister is very talkative at home, but she becomes quiet and shy when she meets new people.","t":"我妹妹在家裡很愛說話，但遇到陌生人時就變得安靜又害羞。"},{"w":"slang","p":"n.","d":"very informal words used by a particular group","c":"俚語","s":"Teenagers often use slang that their parents do not understand, so family conversations can be confusing.","t":"青少年常用父母聽不懂的俚語，所以家庭對話可能會讓人摸不著頭緒。"},{"w":"acronym","p":"n.","d":"a word made from the first letters of other words","c":"首字母縮略字","s":"\"NASA\" is an acronym that people say as one word, and many students do not know what the letters stand for.","t":"「NASA」是一個人們當作一個字來唸的首字母縮略字，許多學生不知道那些字母代表什麼。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (conjure – silence)","cards":[{"w":"conjure","p":"v.","d":"to make a picture or idea appear in someone's mind","c":"使浮現；變出","s":"The word \"headline\" conjure images of big black letters, but today most headlines appear on small phone screens.","t":"「頭條」這個字會讓人聯想到大大的黑色字體，但如今大多數標題都出現在小小的手機螢幕上。"},{"w":"decry","p":"v.","d":"to say publicly that something is bad","c":"公開譴責；抨擊","s":"Many teachers decry the use of phones in class, but some argue that phones can be useful learning tools.","t":"許多老師抨擊在課堂上使用手機，但也有人認為手機可以是有用的學習工具。"},{"w":"denigrate","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is not good or important","c":"詆毀；貶低","s":"The new advert openly denigrate rival brands, so many viewers complained that it was unfair and unkind.","t":"那則新廣告公然貶低競爭品牌，所以許多觀眾抱怨它不公平又不厚道。"},{"w":"disavow","p":"v.","d":"to say you are not connected with something","c":"否認（與…有關）；撇清","s":"The party quickly disavow the fake website, because it was spreading lies in the party's name.","t":"該黨很快就撇清與那個假網站的關係，因為它以該黨的名義散播謊言。"},{"w":"discount","p":"v.","d":"to decide that something is not important or true","c":"不理會；不全信","s":"You should not discount a story just because you dislike the newspaper, so always look at the evidence first.","t":"你不應該只因為不喜歡那家報紙就不採信一則報導，所以一定要先看證據。"},{"w":"disparage","p":"v.","d":"to speak about someone in a way that shows no respect","c":"貶損；輕視","s":"The host often disparage his guests to get laughs, but many viewers found his jokes cruel rather than funny.","t":"那位主持人常常貶損來賓來博取笑聲，但許多觀眾覺得他的笑話殘忍而不好笑。"},{"w":"divulge","p":"v.","d":"to tell secret information","c":"洩漏；透露","s":"The reporter refused to divulge her source, even though the court threatened to fine her.","t":"那位記者拒絕透露她的消息來源，即使法院威脅要對她罰款。"},{"w":"downplay","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less important than it is","c":"淡化；輕描淡寫","s":"The company tried to downplay the data leak, but customers were angry when they learned how many accounts were affected.","t":"那家公司試圖淡化資料外洩事件，但顧客得知有多少帳號受影響時非常憤怒。"},{"w":"dramatise","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem more exciting or serious than it is","c":"誇大；戲劇化","s":"The video dramatise a small argument between neighbours, so it looked like a violent fight.","t":"那段影片把鄰居間的小爭執戲劇化了，所以看起來像一場暴力衝突。"},{"w":"embroil","p":"v.","d":"to involve someone in a difficult situation","c":"使捲入（糾紛）","s":"The singer became embroil in a copyright battle, and her new album was delayed for over a year.","t":"那位歌手捲入了一場版權糾紛，她的新專輯延遲了一年多。"},{"w":"equivocate","p":"v.","d":"to avoid giving a clear answer","c":"含糊其辭；支吾搪塞","s":"The minister equivocate when reporters asked about the budget, so nobody knew whether the new hospital would be built.","t":"記者詢問預算時部長含糊其辭，所以沒有人知道新醫院會不會蓋。"},{"w":"garble","p":"v.","d":"to mix up a message so it is hard to understand","c":"使混亂不清；曲解","s":"The phone line was poor and his message was garble, so I could only understand a few words.","t":"電話訊號很差，他的訊息斷斷續續聽不清楚，所以我只聽懂了幾個字。"},{"w":"glamorise","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem more attractive than it really is","c":"美化；使有魅力","s":"Some films glamorise smoking, so young viewers may think it looks cool rather than dangerous.","t":"有些電影美化抽菸，所以年輕觀眾可能會覺得那很酷而不是危險。"},{"w":"hijack","p":"v.","d":"to take control of something for your own purposes","c":"劫持；挾持（議題）","s":"A small group hijack the online discussion about school lunches, and soon everyone was arguing about politics instead.","t":"一小群人挾持了關於學校午餐的網路討論，很快大家都改成在吵政治。"},{"w":"insinuate","p":"v.","d":"to suggest something bad in an indirect way","c":"暗示；影射","s":"The article insinuate that the athlete had cheated, but it did not give any real evidence.","t":"那篇文章暗示那位運動員作弊，但沒有提出任何真正的證據。"},{"w":"misconstrue","p":"v.","d":"to understand something wrongly","c":"誤解；曲解","s":"My friend misconstrue my joke as an insult, so I explained what I meant and apologised.","t":"我朋友把我的玩笑誤解成侮辱，所以我解釋了我的意思並道歉。"},{"w":"misrepresent","p":"v.","d":"to describe someone or something falsely","c":"歪曲；不實地陳述","s":"The short clip misrepresent the scientist's views, because it left out the part where she explained her doubts.","t":"那段短片歪曲了那位科學家的觀點，因為它刪掉了她解釋自己疑慮的部分。"},{"w":"muddle","p":"v.","d":"to mix things up and cause confusion","c":"使混亂；弄混","s":"The two reports used different numbers, so they muddle readers who wanted to know the real cost.","t":"兩份報告使用了不同的數字，所以讓想知道實際花費的讀者一頭霧水。"},{"w":"obfuscate","p":"v.","d":"to make something deliberately unclear","c":"使模糊；混淆","s":"The contract used long, difficult words to obfuscate the hidden fees, so few customers noticed them.","t":"那份合約使用又長又難的字來混淆隱藏費用，所以很少顧客注意到。"},{"w":"pander","p":"v.","d":"to give people what they want even if it is wrong","c":"迎合；討好","s":"Some websites pander to readers' fears, because frightening stories get more clicks than calm ones.","t":"有些網站迎合讀者的恐懼，因為嚇人的報導比冷靜的報導獲得更多點擊。"},{"w":"placate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone less angry","c":"安撫；平息怒氣","s":"The manager offered free tickets to placate the angry fans, but many still demanded a full refund.","t":"經理提供免費門票來安撫憤怒的球迷，但許多人仍要求全額退款。"},{"w":"profess","p":"v.","d":"to claim something, often falsely","c":"聲稱；自稱","s":"He profess to be an expert on health, but he had no medical training and his advice was dangerous.","t":"他自稱是健康專家，但他沒有受過醫學訓練，他的建議很危險。"},{"w":"relay","p":"v.","d":"to pass a message from one person to another","c":"轉達；轉播","s":"The teacher asked me to relay the message to my classmates, because the school website was not working.","t":"老師要我把訊息轉達給同學，因為學校網站故障了。"},{"w":"repudiate","p":"v.","d":"to say officially that something is not true","c":"駁斥；否認","s":"The scientist publicly repudiate the claims made in the video, and she explained why they were wrong.","t":"那位科學家公開駁斥影片中的說法，並解釋為什麼它們是錯的。"},{"w":"silence","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from speaking or expressing opinions","c":"使沉默；壓制","s":"The government tried to silence critics by closing newspapers, but people continued to share news online.","t":"政府試圖關閉報社來壓制批評者的聲音，但人們繼續在網路上分享新聞。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (stigmatise – rebuke)","cards":[{"w":"stigmatise","p":"v.","d":"to treat a group of people as shameful","c":"污名化","s":"News reports should not stigmatise people with mental illness, because this stops many of them from asking for help.","t":"新聞報導不應該污名化有精神疾病的人，因為這會讓他們許多人不敢求助。"},{"w":"trivialise","p":"v.","d":"to make something serious seem unimportant","c":"輕忽；使顯得瑣碎","s":"The comedian's joke trivialise the flood, so families who had lost their homes were deeply upset.","t":"那位喜劇演員的笑話輕忽了水災的嚴重性，所以失去家園的家庭非常難過。"},{"w":"undercut","p":"v.","d":"to make something weaker or less effective","c":"削弱；削價競爭","s":"The small mistakes in the report undercut its main argument, so readers began to doubt everything else in it.","t":"報告中的小錯誤削弱了它的主要論點，所以讀者開始懷疑裡面的其他一切。"},{"w":"unmask","p":"v.","d":"to show the truth about someone who was hiding it","c":"揭穿；揭露真面目","s":"Journalists unmask the person behind the fake charity, and the police arrested him a week later.","t":"記者們揭穿了假慈善機構背後的人，警方一週後逮捕了他。"},{"w":"vilify","p":"v.","d":"to say very bad things about someone, often unfairly","c":"詆毀；中傷","s":"Some newspapers vilify the young footballer after one mistake, but his team continued to support him.","t":"有些報紙在那位年輕足球員失誤一次後就大肆抨擊他，但他的球隊仍然支持他。"},{"w":"vouch","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good or true","c":"擔保；保證","s":"I can vouch for this website, because I have used it for years and its information has always been accurate.","t":"我可以擔保這個網站，因為我用了好幾年，它的資訊一直都很準確。"},{"w":"belie","p":"v.","d":"to give a false idea of something","c":"掩飾；使人誤解","s":"Her calm voice belie how nervous she really felt, so the audience thought she was very confident.","t":"她平靜的聲音掩飾了她真實的緊張，所以觀眾以為她非常有自信。"},{"w":"curate","p":"v.","d":"to choose and organise items for people to see","c":"策劃；篩選整理","s":"The app curate news from many sources, but it is still important to check who wrote each story.","t":"那個應用程式篩選整理來自許多來源的新聞，但查看每則報導是誰寫的仍然很重要。"},{"w":"demonise","p":"v.","d":"to describe a person or group as evil","c":"妖魔化","s":"Politicians sometimes demonise their opponents to win votes, but this makes it harder for people to work together.","t":"政治人物有時會妖魔化對手來贏得選票，但這會讓人們更難合作。"},{"w":"embolden","p":"v.","d":"to make someone braver or more confident","c":"使大膽；壯膽","s":"The large number of likes embolden him to post even ruder comments, so his friends finally told him to stop.","t":"大量的按讚讓他更大膽，發了更無禮的留言，所以他的朋友終於叫他住手。"},{"w":"enthral","p":"v.","d":"to hold someone's attention completely","c":"使著迷；迷住","s":"The storyteller enthral the children with her tales of dragons, and nobody moved until the very end.","t":"那位說故事的人用她的龍的故事迷住了孩子們，直到最後都沒有人動一下。"},{"w":"foment","p":"v.","d":"to cause trouble or violence","c":"煽動；挑起","s":"The fake posts were designed to foment anger between the two groups, so police warned people not to share them.","t":"那些假貼文旨在挑起兩個群體之間的憤怒，所以警方警告民眾不要分享。"},{"w":"monetise","p":"v.","d":"to earn money from something","c":"使獲利；變現","s":"Many creators monetise their videos through adverts, but they need thousands of viewers before they earn much.","t":"許多創作者透過廣告讓影片變現，但他們需要上千名觀眾才能賺到不少錢。"},{"w":"overhear","p":"v.","d":"to hear something by accident","c":"無意中聽到","s":"I overhear two students talking about the exam, but I soon realised that their information was wrong.","t":"我無意中聽到兩個學生在討論考試，但我很快就發現他們的資訊是錯的。"},{"w":"recant","p":"v.","d":"to say publicly that you no longer believe something you said","c":"公開撤回（說法）","s":"The witness recant her story in court, so the journalists who had reported it had to publish corrections.","t":"那位證人在法庭上撤回了她的說法，所以報導過的記者必須刊登更正。"},{"w":"sabotage","p":"v.","d":"to damage something on purpose to stop it working","c":"蓄意破壞","s":"Someone sabotage the school's website before the vote, so students could not see the candidates' speeches.","t":"有人在投票前蓄意破壞了學校網站，所以學生看不到候選人的演講。"},{"w":"subvert","p":"v.","d":"to weaken a system or belief","c":"顛覆；破壞","s":"False news can subvert democracy, because voters make choices based on information that is not true.","t":"假新聞可能顛覆民主，因為選民根據不實的資訊做出選擇。"},{"w":"summon","p":"v.","d":"to officially order someone to come","c":"傳喚；召集","s":"The editor was summon to court after the newspaper published secret documents, but she said the public had a right to know.","t":"報社刊登機密文件後，總編輯被傳喚出庭，但她說大眾有知的權利。"},{"w":"whitewash","p":"v.","d":"to hide mistakes or bad facts","c":"粉飾；掩蓋","s":"The report tried to whitewash the company's safety problems, but workers later told reporters what had really happened.","t":"那份報告試圖粉飾公司的安全問題，但員工後來告訴記者到底發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"chastise","p":"v.","d":"to criticise someone strongly","c":"嚴厲斥責","s":"The coach chastise the players for posting rude comments online, and he made them apologise to the other team.","t":"教練嚴厲斥責球員在網路上發布無禮留言，並要他們向對手道歉。"},{"w":"coax","p":"v.","d":"to gently persuade someone","c":"哄勸；勸誘","s":"The reporter coax the shy girl into telling her story, and her words touched thousands of viewers.","t":"那位記者溫柔地勸那個害羞的女孩說出她的故事，而她的話感動了數千名觀眾。"},{"w":"infiltrate","p":"v.","d":"to secretly join a group to get information","c":"滲透；潛入","s":"The journalist infiltrate the fake news group by pretending to be a new member, and she recorded how they planned their posts.","t":"那名記者假裝成新成員潛入了那個假新聞團體，並記錄下他們如何策劃貼文。"},{"w":"orchestrate","p":"v.","d":"to organise something carefully, often secretly","c":"精心策劃；暗中安排","s":"The protest looked natural, but it was actually orchestrate by a company that wanted to stop the new law.","t":"那場抗議看起來很自然，但其實是一家想阻止新法的公司精心策劃的。"},{"w":"perpetrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something wrong or harmful","c":"犯下（罪行）；做（壞事）","s":"The fraud was perpetrate by a group who sent fake messages from the bank, so many elderly people lost their savings.","t":"那起詐騙是由一個冒充銀行發送假訊息的集團犯下的，所以許多老人失去了積蓄。"},{"w":"rebuke","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone sharply that they have done wrong","c":"指責；訓斥","s":"The judge rebuke the TV station for showing the victim's face, because it put her safety at risk.","t":"法官訓斥那家電視台播出被害人的臉，因為這讓她的安全陷入危險。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (reverberate – quash)","cards":[{"w":"reverberate","p":"v.","d":"to have a strong effect that continues for a long time","c":"產生持續影響；迴響","s":"The scandal reverberate through the entertainment industry for months, and several other stars lost their sponsorship deals.","t":"那起醜聞在娛樂圈持續發酵了好幾個月，其他幾位明星也失去了贊助合約。"},{"w":"usurp","p":"v.","d":"to take someone's position or power without the right","c":"篡奪；奪取","s":"Online videos have usurp the role that television once played, so many young people never watch the evening news.","t":"網路影片已經取代奪走了電視曾扮演的角色，所以許多年輕人從不看晚間新聞。"},{"w":"weaponise","p":"v.","d":"to use something as a way to attack others","c":"將…武器化","s":"Some groups weaponise social media to attack journalists, and several reporters have had to close their accounts.","t":"有些團體把社群媒體武器化來攻擊記者，好幾位記者不得不關閉帳號。"},{"w":"woo","p":"v.","d":"to try to get someone's support","c":"爭取；拉攏","s":"Both candidates tried to woo young voters with short videos, because they knew most students do not watch TV debates.","t":"兩位候選人都試圖用短影片拉攏年輕選民，因為他們知道大多數學生不看電視辯論。"},{"w":"admonish","p":"v.","d":"to warn or criticise someone firmly","c":"告誡；責備","s":"The teacher admonish the class for sharing a classmate's photo without permission, and she explained why it was harmful.","t":"老師告誡全班未經同意就分享同學的照片，並解釋為什麼那是有害的。"},{"w":"blur","p":"v.","d":"to make the difference between things less clear","c":"使模糊；混淆界線","s":"Sponsored videos blur the line between advice and advertising, so viewers may not realise they are being sold something.","t":"業配影片模糊了建議和廣告之間的界線，所以觀眾可能沒發現有人在向他們推銷東西。"},{"w":"capitulate","p":"v.","d":"to stop resisting and agree to something","c":"屈服；讓步","s":"The platform finally capitulate to public pressure and removed the harmful videos, but critics said it had acted too slowly.","t":"那個平台最終屈服於輿論壓力，刪除了有害影片，但批評者說它行動太慢了。"},{"w":"collude","p":"v.","d":"to work together secretly to cheat others","c":"勾結；串通","s":"The two companies collude to keep prices high, but a journalist found their emails and reported the story.","t":"那兩家公司串通維持高價，但一名記者找到了他們的電子郵件並報導了此事。"},{"w":"conflate","p":"v.","d":"to wrongly treat two different things as the same","c":"混為一談","s":"Many people conflate opinion with fact, so they believe that a strong feeling must also be true.","t":"許多人把意見和事實混為一談，所以他們相信強烈的感覺也一定是真的。"},{"w":"defuse","p":"v.","d":"to make a tense situation calmer","c":"緩和；化解","s":"The teacher defuse the argument by asking both students to explain their views calmly, and soon they were laughing.","t":"老師請兩位學生冷靜地說明各自的觀點來化解爭吵，很快他們就笑了起來。"},{"w":"delude","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something that is not true","c":"欺騙；使誤信","s":"Don't delude yourself that you can study well while watching videos, because your brain cannot focus on both.","t":"別欺騙自己說你能邊看影片邊好好讀書，因為你的大腦無法同時專注兩件事。"},{"w":"emanate","p":"v.","d":"to come from a particular source","c":"發出；源自","s":"The rumour seemed to emanate from a single anonymous account, but it soon spread to thousands of users.","t":"那則謠言似乎源自一個匿名帳號，但很快就傳到了數千名使用者那裡。"},{"w":"enunciate","p":"v.","d":"to say words clearly","c":"清楚地發音","s":"Good news presenters enunciate every word, so even viewers with poor hearing can follow the news.","t":"好的新聞主播會把每個字咬字清楚，所以即使聽力不好的觀眾也能聽懂新聞。"},{"w":"eschew","p":"v.","d":"to avoid something on purpose","c":"刻意避開；避免","s":"The newspaper eschew celebrity gossip, because it wants to focus on serious local and international news.","t":"那份報紙刻意避開名人八卦，因為它想專注於嚴肅的地方和國際新聞。"},{"w":"exonerate","p":"v.","d":"to show officially that someone is not guilty","c":"證明無罪；洗清罪名","s":"New video evidence exonerate the young man, but by then his photo had already been shared as a \"criminal\" online.","t":"新的影片證據證明那位年輕人無罪，但那時他的照片早已被當作「罪犯」在網路上流傳。"},{"w":"feign","p":"v.","d":"to pretend to feel something","c":"假裝","s":"He feign surprise when he saw the results, but he had already read them online that morning.","t":"他看到結果時假裝驚訝，但他那天早上已經在網路上看過了。"},{"w":"flout","p":"v.","d":"to break a rule openly","c":"公然違反","s":"Some influencers flout advertising rules by hiding paid posts, so the government is planning heavier fines.","t":"有些網紅藉由隱瞞業配貼文公然違反廣告規定，所以政府打算加重罰款。"},{"w":"interject","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt with a comment","c":"插話；插嘴","s":"During the debate one student kept trying to interject, so the teacher reminded everyone to wait for their turn.","t":"辯論時有位學生一直想插話，所以老師提醒大家等輪到自己再說。"},{"w":"lambast","p":"v.","d":"to criticise someone very strongly","c":"嚴厲抨擊","s":"Critics lambast the film for its poor acting, but audiences loved it and it earned a lot of money.","t":"影評人嚴厲抨擊那部電影演技很差，但觀眾很喜歡，它賺了很多錢。"},{"w":"languish","p":"v.","d":"to stay in a bad situation for a long time","c":"受困；被冷落","s":"The important report languish on the minister's desk for months, so the public never learned about the problems in time.","t":"那份重要報告在部長桌上被冷落了好幾個月，所以大眾沒能及時得知那些問題。"},{"w":"shroud","p":"v.","d":"to cover or hide something","c":"籠罩；隱藏","s":"The cause of the accident remains shroud in mystery, because the company refuses to release the video.","t":"那起事故的原因仍籠罩在謎團中，因為公司拒絕公開影片。"},{"w":"malign","p":"v.","d":"to say unfair and harmful things about someone","c":"中傷；誹謗","s":"The actress said she had been malign by fake stories, and she asked her fans to stop sharing them.","t":"那位女演員說她被假新聞中傷，並請粉絲不要再分享。"},{"w":"muster","p":"v.","d":"to gather courage, strength or support","c":"鼓起（勇氣）；召集","s":"She finally muster the courage to report the cyberbullying, and the school took action the same day.","t":"她終於鼓起勇氣舉報網路霸凌，學校當天就採取了行動。"},{"w":"pacify","p":"v.","d":"to make someone calm","c":"使平靜；安撫","s":"The mother tried to pacify her crying baby with a song, but the noise on the train made it very difficult.","t":"那位母親試著用一首歌安撫哭鬧的寶寶，但火車上的噪音讓這件事變得很困難。"},{"w":"quash","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from continuing","c":"平息；壓制","s":"The company quickly posted a video to quash the rumours about closing, and its share price rose the next day.","t":"那家公司很快發布影片來平息關於倒閉的謠言，隔天股價就上漲了。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (ramble – factual)","cards":[{"w":"ramble","p":"v.","d":"to talk for a long time in a confused way","c":"漫無邊際地閒扯","s":"The speaker ramble for twenty minutes without making a clear point, so half the audience started checking their phones.","t":"那位講者東拉西扯了二十分鐘卻沒講出重點，所以一半的聽眾開始看手機。"},{"w":"retort","p":"v.","d":"to reply quickly and angrily","c":"反駁；回嘴","s":"When the reporter asked about the mistake, the coach retort that the referee was to blame, and he walked away.","t":"記者問到那個失誤時，教練反駁說是裁判的錯，然後就走開了。"},{"w":"stymie","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from making progress","c":"阻礙；使受挫","s":"Slow internet stymie the students' research, so the teacher gave them extra time to finish the project.","t":"網路太慢阻礙了學生的研究，所以老師給他們額外的時間完成專題。"},{"w":"waver","p":"v.","d":"to be unable to decide; to become less certain","c":"動搖；猶豫不決","s":"Her support for the plan began to waver after she read the critics' arguments, so she asked for more information.","t":"讀了批評者的論點後，她對該計畫的支持開始動搖，所以她要求更多資訊。"},{"w":"understate","p":"v.","d":"to describe something as smaller than it really is","c":"輕描淡寫；少報","s":"The official report understate the number of people affected by the flood, so less help was sent than was needed.","t":"官方報告少報了受水災影響的人數，所以送去的援助比需要的少。"},{"w":"romanticise","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem better than it really is","c":"浪漫化；理想化","s":"Many films romanticise life in big cities, but in reality young workers often struggle with high rent and long hours.","t":"許多電影美化大城市的生活，但現實中年輕上班族常為高房租和長工時所苦。"},{"w":"scapegoat","p":"v.","d":"to blame someone unfairly for others' mistakes","c":"使成為代罪羔羊","s":"The company scapegoat a junior employee for the data leak, although managers had ignored the warnings for months.","t":"公司讓一名基層員工當代罪羔羊承擔資料外洩的責任，儘管主管們已忽視警告好幾個月。"},{"w":"incriminate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone seem guilty","c":"使顯得有罪；牽連","s":"The messages on his phone incriminate him, because they showed that he had planned the fake reviews.","t":"他手機裡的訊息顯示他有罪，因為那些訊息證明他策劃了假評論。"},{"w":"insist","p":"v.","d":"to say firmly that something is true or must happen","c":"堅持；堅稱","s":"The influencer insist that the photos were not edited, but experts showed clear signs that they had been changed.","t":"那位網紅堅稱照片沒有修過，但專家指出了明顯被修改的跡象。"},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to state something officially or clearly","c":"宣布；聲明","s":"The organisers declare the event a success, although many people complained about the long queues.","t":"主辦單位宣布活動很成功，儘管許多人抱怨排隊太久。"},{"w":"utter","p":"v.","d":"to say something","c":"說出；發出（聲音）","s":"He did not utter a single word during the meeting, so his manager later asked whether he disagreed with the plan.","t":"他在會議中一個字都沒說，所以經理後來問他是否不同意這個計畫。"},{"w":"voice","p":"v.","d":"to express an opinion or feeling","c":"表達；說出","s":"Several worried parents voice concerns about the new app, because it secretly collected children's location data.","t":"好幾位憂心的家長表達了對那個新應用程式的擔憂，因為它偷偷收集孩子的位置資料。"},{"w":"muzzle","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from speaking freely","c":"封口；壓制言論","s":"The new law could muzzle the press, because journalists may be fined for reporting on government mistakes.","t":"新法可能會封住媒體的口，因為記者可能因報導政府的錯誤而被罰款。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you did something wrong","c":"承認；坦白","s":"The student confess that he had copied the essay from a website, so the teacher let him write it again.","t":"那位學生坦承他從網站上抄了那篇作文，所以老師讓他重寫。"},{"w":"accusatory","p":"adj.","d":"suggesting that someone has done wrong","c":"指責的；控訴的","s":"The comment sounded accusatory, so my friend felt hurt even though I had only asked a simple question.","t":"那句留言聽起來帶有指責的意味，所以即使我只是問了個簡單的問題，我朋友還是覺得受傷。"},{"w":"adamant","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to change your opinion","c":"堅定不移的；堅持的","s":"The author was adamant that the story was true, but she could not provide any documents to prove it.","t":"那位作者堅稱那個故事是真的，但她提不出任何文件來證明。"},{"w":"alarmist","p":"adj.","d":"making people worried without good reason","c":"危言聳聽的","s":"The alarmist headline said that all phones cause cancer, but the study it described was very small and uncertain.","t":"那個危言聳聽的標題說所有手機都會致癌，但它所描述的研究規模很小又不確定。"},{"w":"complicit","p":"adj.","d":"involved with others in doing something wrong","c":"共謀的；有共犯責任的","s":"By sharing the cruel video, many users became complicit in the bullying, although they did not create it.","t":"許多使用者分享那段殘忍的影片，雖然不是他們拍的，卻也成了霸凌的共犯。"},{"w":"culpable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving blame","c":"應受責備的；有罪責的","s":"The court found the website culpable for the damage, because it had published the false story without checking.","t":"法院判定那個網站對損害負有責任，因為它未經查證就刊登了不實報導。"},{"w":"deceitful","p":"adj.","d":"trying to make people believe things that are false","c":"欺詐的；不誠實的","s":"The deceitful seller used photos of a different house, so the family was shocked when they saw the real one.","t":"那個不誠實的賣家使用了另一棟房子的照片，所以那家人看到真正的房子時大吃一驚。"},{"w":"derogatory","p":"adj.","d":"showing a very poor opinion of someone","c":"貶損的；不敬的","s":"The player used a derogatory word about his opponent, and the league banned him for three matches.","t":"那名球員對對手使用了貶損的字眼，聯盟禁賽他三場。"},{"w":"disingenuous","p":"adj.","d":"pretending to be honest when you are not","c":"不真誠的；虛偽的","s":"It is disingenuous to say the advert is \"just information\", because the company clearly wants to sell its product.","t":"說那則廣告「只是資訊」是不真誠的，因為那家公司顯然想賣它的產品。"},{"w":"dismissive","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think something is not important","c":"輕蔑的；不屑一顧的","s":"The manager was dismissive of the customer's complaint, so she posted a long review online that many people read.","t":"經理對顧客的投訴不屑一顧，所以她在網路上發表了一篇很多人讀的長篇評論。"},{"w":"emotive","p":"adj.","d":"causing strong feelings","c":"引起強烈情感的","s":"The charity used emotive pictures of hungry children, and donations increased sharply within a week.","t":"那個慈善機構使用了飢餓兒童的觸動情感的照片，一週內捐款大幅增加。"},{"w":"factual","p":"adj.","d":"based on facts, not opinions","c":"根據事實的；事實性的","s":"The report contained several factual errors, so the newspaper had to correct the dates and names the next day.","t":"那篇報導有好幾處事實錯誤，所以報社隔天必須更正日期和人名。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (far-fetched – vociferous)","cards":[{"w":"far-fetched","p":"adj.","d":"very unlikely to be true","c":"牽強的；難以置信的","s":"His explanation sounded far-fetched, because nobody believes that a dog could really eat a whole laptop.","t":"他的解釋聽起來很牽強，因為沒有人相信一隻狗真的能吃掉一整台筆電。"},{"w":"fictitious","p":"adj.","d":"invented and not real","c":"虛構的；捏造的","s":"The website used fictitious names for its \"doctors\", so none of them could be found in any medical records.","t":"那個網站為它的「醫生」使用虛構的名字，所以在任何醫療紀錄中都找不到他們。"},{"w":"forthright","p":"adj.","d":"saying clearly and honestly what you think","c":"坦率的；直言不諱的","s":"The new principal is forthright about the school's problems, and parents appreciate that she does not hide bad news.","t":"新校長對學校的問題直言不諱，家長們很欣賞她不隱瞞壞消息。"},{"w":"gratuitous","p":"adj.","d":"not necessary and often harmful","c":"不必要的；無端的","s":"The film was full of gratuitous violence, so many parents decided it was not suitable for their children.","t":"那部電影充滿不必要的暴力，所以許多家長認為它不適合孩子看。"},{"w":"groundless","p":"adj.","d":"not based on facts or reasons","c":"毫無根據的","s":"The fears about the new phone tower were groundless, but the rumours spread quickly in the village anyway.","t":"對新基地台的恐懼是毫無根據的，但謠言還是在村子裡迅速散播開來。"},{"w":"ill-informed","p":"adj.","d":"having wrong or too little information","c":"消息不靈通的；無知的","s":"Many ill-informed comments appeared under the article, because people reacted to the headline without reading the story.","t":"文章下方出現許多不了解狀況的留言，因為人們沒讀內容就對標題做出反應。"},{"w":"impressionable","p":"adj.","d":"easily influenced by others","c":"易受影響的","s":"Young children are very impressionable, so they may copy dangerous stunts they see in online videos.","t":"年幼的孩子很容易受影響，所以他們可能會模仿網路影片中看到的危險特技。"},{"w":"incontrovertible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to argue against","c":"無可辯駁的；不容置疑的","s":"The video gave incontrovertible proof that the driver had run the red light, so he finally admitted his mistake.","t":"那段影片提供了無可辯駁的證據，證明司機闖了紅燈，所以他終於承認錯誤。"},{"w":"indignant","p":"adj.","d":"angry because something seems unfair","c":"憤慨的；義憤填膺的","s":"The students were indignant when the school cancelled their trip without explanation, so they wrote a letter to the principal.","t":"學校無故取消他們的旅行時，學生們憤憤不平，所以他們寫了一封信給校長。"},{"w":"informative","p":"adj.","d":"giving useful information","c":"有益的；資訊豐富的","s":"The museum's website is very informative, and it helped me find all the facts I needed for my history project.","t":"博物館的網站資訊非常豐富，它幫我找到歷史專題所需的所有資料。"},{"w":"jaded","p":"adj.","d":"bored or tired because you have seen too much of something","c":"厭倦的；麻木的","s":"After years of political scandals, many voters feel jaded, so they no longer pay attention to the news.","t":"經過多年的政治醜聞，許多選民感到麻木厭倦，所以他們不再關注新聞。"},{"w":"lurid","p":"adj.","d":"shocking and full of unpleasant details","c":"駭人聽聞的；聳動的","s":"The magazine printed lurid details about the crime, but the victim's family said this caused them great pain.","t":"那本雜誌刊登了犯罪案駭人聽聞的細節，但被害人家屬說這讓他們非常痛苦。"},{"w":"one-sided","p":"adj.","d":"showing only one point of view","c":"片面的；一面倒的","s":"The documentary was one-sided, because it interviewed only the factory owners and none of the local farmers.","t":"那部紀錄片很片面，因為它只採訪了工廠老闆，沒有採訪任何當地農民。"},{"w":"opinionated","p":"adj.","d":"having strong views and expressing them too often","c":"固執己見的","s":"My uncle is very opinionated about politics, so family dinners often end in loud arguments.","t":"我叔叔對政治非常固執己見，所以家庭聚餐常以大聲爭吵收場。"},{"w":"outspoken","p":"adj.","d":"saying exactly what you think in public","c":"直言不諱的；敢言的","s":"The outspoken student spoke against the new rule at the meeting, and many classmates later thanked her for her courage.","t":"那位敢言的學生在會議上反對新規定，後來許多同學感謝她的勇氣。"},{"w":"pejorative","p":"adj.","d":"expressing disapproval or a low opinion","c":"貶義的","s":"\"Nerd\" was once a pejorative word, but today many young people use it proudly to describe themselves.","t":"「書呆子」曾經是一個貶義的字，但如今許多年輕人驕傲地用它來形容自己。"},{"w":"populist","p":"adj.","d":"claiming to support ordinary people against the elite","c":"民粹主義的","s":"The populist leader promised simple solutions to complex problems, and many frustrated voters liked his message.","t":"那位民粹主義的領袖承諾用簡單的方法解決複雜的問題，許多不滿的選民喜歡他的訴求。"},{"w":"pretentious","p":"adj.","d":"trying to seem more important or clever than you are","c":"自命不凡的；做作的","s":"The review was full of long, pretentious words, so most readers could not understand whether the critic liked the film.","t":"那篇影評充滿又長又做作的字眼，所以大多數讀者看不懂影評人到底喜不喜歡那部電影。"},{"w":"salacious","p":"adj.","d":"containing too much interest in sexual or shocking details","c":"淫穢的；低俗煽情的","s":"Cheap tabloids often print salacious stories about celebrities, because such stories usually sell many more copies.","t":"廉價小報常刊登關於名人的低俗煽情的報導，因為這類報導通常賣得好得多。"},{"w":"scathing","p":"adj.","d":"criticising very strongly","c":"尖刻的；嚴厲的","s":"The critic wrote a scathing review of the restaurant, and within a month the owner had changed the whole menu.","t":"那位評論家寫了一篇尖刻的餐廳評論，一個月內老闆就換掉了整份菜單。"},{"w":"self-serving","p":"adj.","d":"done mainly to help yourself","c":"自私自利的；為自己打算的","s":"The company's apology seemed self-serving, because it spent more time praising its products than helping the victims.","t":"那家公司的道歉似乎是在為自己打算，因為它花在稱讚產品的時間比幫助受害者還多。"},{"w":"trite","p":"adj.","d":"used so often that it is no longer interesting","c":"陳腐的；老套的","s":"Her speech was full of trite phrases like \"follow your dreams\", so the audience soon lost interest.","t":"她的演講充滿像「追隨你的夢想」這樣老套的句子，所以聽眾很快就失去興趣。"},{"w":"truthful","p":"adj.","d":"honest and telling the truth","c":"誠實的；真實的","s":"Please be truthful in your survey answers, because the results will help the school improve its services.","t":"請誠實回答問卷，因為結果將幫助學校改善服務。"},{"w":"vocal","p":"adj.","d":"expressing opinions strongly and publicly","c":"直言的；大聲疾呼的","s":"Parents have been very vocal about the dangers of the busy road, and the city has finally agreed to add a crossing.","t":"家長們對那條繁忙道路的危險一直大聲疾呼，市政府終於同意增設行人穿越道。"},{"w":"vociferous","p":"adj.","d":"expressing opinions loudly and forcefully","c":"大聲疾呼的；喧嚷的","s":"The plan faced vociferous opposition from local residents, so the council decided to hold another public meeting.","t":"該計畫遭到當地居民強烈反對，所以議會決定再舉行一次公聽會。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (watertight – allegation)","cards":[{"w":"watertight","p":"adj.","d":"so strong it cannot be questioned","c":"無懈可擊的；嚴密的","s":"The lawyer's argument seemed watertight, but the journalist found one small mistake that changed everything.","t":"那位律師的論點看似無懈可擊，但那名記者找到一個改變一切的小錯誤。"},{"w":"wilful","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, knowing it is wrong","c":"蓄意的；故意的","s":"Sharing a story you know is false is wilful deception, so it is much worse than making an honest mistake.","t":"分享你明知是假的消息是蓄意的欺騙，所以比無心之過嚴重得多。"},{"w":"offensive","p":"adj.","d":"rude in a way that upsets people","c":"冒犯的；無禮的","s":"The joke was offensive to many people, so the comedian apologised and removed the video from his channel.","t":"那個笑話冒犯了許多人，所以那位喜劇演員道歉並從他的頻道上撤下影片。"},{"w":"outlandish","p":"adj.","d":"very strange and unusual","c":"古怪的；荒誕的","s":"The website made outlandish claims about a fruit that could cure every disease, but no scientist supported them.","t":"那個網站對一種能治百病的水果做出荒誕的說法，但沒有科學家支持。"},{"w":"preposterous","p":"adj.","d":"completely unreasonable or silly","c":"荒謬的；可笑的","s":"The idea that the earth is flat is preposterous, but some videos promoting it still get millions of views.","t":"地球是平的這個想法很荒謬，但一些宣揚它的影片仍然獲得數百萬次觀看。"},{"w":"ludicrous","p":"adj.","d":"so silly that it makes people laugh","c":"荒唐可笑的","s":"The price of the concert tickets was ludicrous, so many fans decided to watch the livestream instead.","t":"演唱會門票的價格貴得離譜，所以許多粉絲決定改看直播。"},{"w":"suspicious","p":"adj.","d":"making you think something is wrong","c":"可疑的；令人懷疑的","s":"I received a suspicious email asking for my bank password, so I deleted it and reported it to the bank.","t":"我收到一封要我提供銀行密碼的可疑電子郵件，所以我刪除了它並通報銀行。"},{"w":"topical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to things happening now","c":"時事性的；熱門話題的","s":"Our English teacher likes to discuss topical issues in class, so we often read news articles from the same week.","t":"我們的英文老師喜歡在課堂上討論時事議題，所以我們常讀同一週的新聞報導。"},{"w":"long-winded","p":"adj.","d":"too long and boring","c":"冗長的；囉嗦的","s":"The manager's long-winded email took ten minutes to read, but the main point could have been written in two sentences.","t":"經理那封冗長的電子郵件要花十分鐘才讀完，但重點其實兩句話就能寫完。"},{"w":"figurative","p":"adj.","d":"not using words in their basic meaning","c":"比喻的；象徵的","s":"\"A sea of faces\" is a figurative expression, so it does not mean that the people were actually in water.","t":"「一片人海」是比喻的說法，所以並不是指人們真的在水裡。"},{"w":"metaphor","p":"n.","d":"describing something by calling it something else","c":"隱喻；暗喻","s":"The writer used the metaphor of a storm to describe the online anger, and readers found the image very powerful.","t":"作者用暴風雨的隱喻來描述網路上的怒火，讀者覺得這個意象非常有力。"},{"w":"buzzword","p":"n.","d":"a fashionable word that becomes very popular","c":"流行術語；時髦用語","s":"\"Sustainable\" has become a buzzword in advertising, but many companies use it without changing how they work.","t":"「永續」已成為廣告中的流行術語，但許多公司使用它卻沒有改變做事的方式。"},{"w":"oratory","p":"n.","d":"the skill of making powerful public speeches","c":"演說技巧；雄辯術","s":"The leader was famous for his oratory, and his speeches made crowds cheer even when his ideas were unclear.","t":"那位領袖以他的演說技巧聞名，即使他的想法不清楚，他的演講也能讓群眾歡呼。"},{"w":"outreach","p":"n.","d":"efforts to give help or information to people","c":"推廣服務；外展活動","s":"The library runs an outreach programme in poor areas, so children without books at home can still read every week.","t":"圖書館在貧困地區舉辦外展推廣計畫，所以家裡沒有書的孩子每週仍能閱讀。"},{"w":"dossier","p":"n.","d":"a set of documents about a person or event","c":"檔案；卷宗","s":"The journalist collected a thick dossier on the company's pollution, and she handed it to the police.","t":"那名記者蒐集了一份關於該公司汙染的厚厚卷宗，並將它交給警方。"},{"w":"communiqué","p":"n.","d":"an official statement, especially after a meeting","c":"公報；官方聲明","s":"The leaders released a joint communiqué after the summit, but it contained few clear promises.","t":"領袖們在高峰會後發表了聯合公報，但內容幾乎沒有明確的承諾。"},{"w":"manifesto","p":"n.","d":"a written statement of a group's aims and beliefs","c":"宣言；政見","s":"The party's manifesto promised free school lunches, so many families decided to vote for it.","t":"該黨的政見承諾提供免費學校午餐，所以許多家庭決定投票給它。"},{"w":"treatise","p":"n.","d":"a long, serious piece of writing on a subject","c":"專著；論文","s":"The professor wrote a treatise on the history of newspapers, and it is still used in universities today.","t":"那位教授寫了一本關於報紙歷史的專著，至今仍在大學裡使用。"},{"w":"anthology","p":"n.","d":"a book of works by different writers","c":"選集；文集","s":"Our teacher gave us an anthology of short stories, and each one was written by a writer from a different country.","t":"老師給了我們一本短篇小說選集，每篇都是由不同國家的作家寫的。"},{"w":"soundbite","p":"n.","d":"a short, memorable phrase taken from a longer speech","c":"（新聞中引用的）精簡名句；原音片段","s":"The news only showed one soundbite from her speech, so viewers missed the important details she explained later.","t":"新聞只播了她演講中的一句原音片段，所以觀眾錯過了她後來解釋的重要細節。"},{"w":"barrage","p":"n.","d":"a large number of things coming at once","c":"接二連三的一大堆；連珠砲","s":"The singer faced a barrage of questions from reporters, but she smiled and answered them one by one.","t":"那位歌手面對記者連珠砲似的提問，但她微笑著一一回答。"},{"w":"torrent","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of something arriving suddenly","c":"洪流；大量湧現","s":"After the video went viral, he received a torrent of messages, and he needed several days to read them all.","t":"影片爆紅後，他收到了如潮水般的訊息，花了好幾天才全部讀完。"},{"w":"glimpse","p":"n.","d":"a quick look or short experience of something","c":"一瞥；短暫的體驗","s":"The documentary gives us a glimpse of life inside a newsroom, and it shows how stressful the job can be.","t":"那部紀錄片讓我們一窺新聞編輯室內的生活，也呈現出這份工作有多大的壓力。"},{"w":"snippet","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of information or conversation","c":"片段；零星資訊","s":"I only heard a snippet of their conversation, so I should not have told everyone what I thought they meant.","t":"我只聽到他們對話的一小片段，所以我不該把我以為的意思告訴大家。"},{"w":"allegation","p":"n.","d":"a claim that someone did something wrong, without proof yet","c":"指控；（未經證實的）說法","s":"The newspaper reported the allegation against the coach, but it made clear that nothing had been proved.","t":"報紙報導了對那位教練的指控，但清楚表明一切尚未獲得證實。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (blunder – uproar)","cards":[{"w":"blunder","p":"n.","d":"a careless and embarrassing mistake","c":"大錯；愚蠢的失誤","s":"The TV station made a big blunder when it showed the wrong winner, and the clip was shared all over the internet.","t":"那家電視台公布錯誤得獎者，犯下了大錯，那段畫面在網路上瘋傳。"},{"w":"bombardment","p":"n.","d":"a very large number of things directed at someone","c":"轟炸；大量湧入","s":"Children face a constant bombardment of adverts online, so it is hard for them to know what they really need.","t":"孩子們在網路上不斷受到廣告轟炸，所以他們很難知道自己真正需要什麼。"},{"w":"caricature","p":"n.","d":"a drawing or description that exaggerates features for humour","c":"諷刺漫畫；誇張描繪","s":"The cartoonist drew a caricature of the president with huge ears, and it appeared on the front of the magazine.","t":"那位漫畫家畫了一幅總統長著大耳朵的諷刺漫畫，它出現在雜誌封面上。"},{"w":"cliché","p":"n.","d":"an idea or phrase used so often it is no longer interesting","c":"陳腔濫調","s":"\"Time flies\" is a cliché, so my teacher told me to find a more original way to start my essay.","t":"「光陰似箭」是陳腔濫調，所以老師要我找一個更有新意的方式來開頭作文。"},{"w":"counterclaim","p":"n.","d":"a claim made to oppose another claim","c":"反訴；反駁的主張","s":"A good essay mentions a counterclaim and then answers it, because this shows that the writer understands both sides.","t":"好的論說文會提出反方主張再加以回應，因為這表示作者了解正反兩面。"},{"w":"demagogue","p":"n.","d":"a leader who wins support by using people's emotions and fears","c":"煽動群眾的政客","s":"The demagogue blamed foreigners for every problem in the country, and his angry speeches attracted large crowds.","t":"那個煽動家把國內的每個問題都歸咎於外國人，他憤怒的演說吸引了大批群眾。"},{"w":"detractor","p":"n.","d":"a person who criticises someone or something","c":"批評者；貶低者","s":"The new app has many fans, but its detractor say that it collects too much personal data.","t":"那款新應用程式有很多粉絲，但批評者說它收集太多個人資料。"},{"w":"euphemism","p":"n.","d":"a polite word used instead of an unpleasant one","c":"委婉語","s":"\"Letting staff go\" is a euphemism for firing people, and the workers were not fooled by the gentle language.","t":"「讓員工離開」是解僱的委婉說法，員工們並沒有被這種溫和的措辭騙到。"},{"w":"fanfare","p":"n.","d":"a lot of public attention and celebration","c":"大肆宣傳；熱烈慶祝","s":"The new phone was launched with great fanfare, but after a few weeks many buyers complained about the battery.","t":"那款新手機在大張旗鼓中上市，但幾週後許多買家抱怨電池問題。"},{"w":"frenzy","p":"n.","d":"a state of wild excitement","c":"狂熱；瘋狂","s":"The rumour of a celebrity wedding caused a media frenzy, and reporters surrounded the hotel for two days.","t":"名人婚禮的傳聞引發了媒體狂熱，記者們包圍那家飯店兩天。"},{"w":"furore","p":"n.","d":"a sudden expression of public anger","c":"騷動；公憤","s":"The decision to cancel the festival caused a furore online, so the organisers changed their minds the next day.","t":"取消音樂節的決定在網路上引起軒然大波，所以主辦單位隔天就改變了主意。"},{"w":"gaffe","p":"n.","d":"an embarrassing mistake in a social situation","c":"失言；出糗","s":"The minister made a gaffe when he forgot the name of the city he was visiting, and the video spread quickly.","t":"部長忘了他正在訪問的城市名稱而失言出糗，那段影片迅速傳開。"},{"w":"hyperbole","p":"n.","d":"a way of speaking that exaggerates a lot","c":"誇飾；誇張法","s":"Saying \"I've told you a million times\" is hyperbole, because nobody really repeats something a million times.","t":"說「我已經跟你講一百萬次了」是一種誇飾，因為沒有人真的會重複一件事一百萬次。"},{"w":"hypocrisy","p":"n.","d":"saying one thing but doing the opposite","c":"虛偽；偽善","s":"People criticised the hypocrisy of the star, because he talked about saving the planet but flew in a private jet every week.","t":"人們批評那位明星的虛偽，因為他談論拯救地球，卻每週搭私人飛機。"},{"w":"innuendo","p":"n.","d":"an indirect remark suggesting something bad","c":"含沙射影的話；影射","s":"The article used innuendo rather than facts, so readers were left thinking the teacher had done something wrong.","t":"那篇文章用含沙射影而非事實，所以讀者以為那位老師做了什麼錯事。"},{"w":"misnomer","p":"n.","d":"a name that does not describe something correctly","c":"用詞不當；名不副實","s":"\"Social media\" can be a misnomer, because many people feel more lonely after using it for hours.","t":"「社群媒體」可能是個名不副實的說法，因為許多人用了幾個小時後反而更覺得孤單。"},{"w":"platitude","p":"n.","d":"a statement that is too obvious and often used","c":"陳腔濫調；老生常談","s":"The company replied with a platitude about \"valuing our customers\", but it did nothing to solve the problem.","t":"那家公司用「重視我們的顧客」這種老生常談回應，卻沒有做任何事來解決問題。"},{"w":"polemic","p":"n.","d":"a strong written or spoken attack on an idea","c":"論戰文章；猛烈抨擊","s":"His book is a polemic against social media, so it does not discuss the benefits that many users enjoy.","t":"他的書是一篇對社群媒體的猛烈抨擊，所以它沒有討論許多使用者享受到的好處。"},{"w":"sarcasm","p":"n.","d":"saying the opposite of what you mean to mock someone","c":"諷刺；挖苦","s":"sarcasm is hard to understand in text messages, so my friend thought I was serious when I was only joking.","t":"反諷在簡訊中很難被理解，所以我只是開玩笑時，我朋友卻以為我是認真的。"},{"w":"scandal","p":"n.","d":"an event that shocks the public because it is wrong","c":"醜聞","s":"The scandal began when a journalist discovered that the charity had spent donations on luxury cars.","t":"那起醜聞始於一名記者發現該慈善機構把捐款花在豪華汽車上。"},{"w":"semblance","p":"n.","d":"a situation that looks like something but may not be","c":"表象；外觀","s":"After the fire, the town slowly returned to some semblance of normal life, and the local paper reopened its office.","t":"火災後，小鎮慢慢恢復了一些正常生活的樣貌，地方報社也重新開張。"},{"w":"spectacle","p":"n.","d":"an event that is exciting or shocking to watch","c":"奇觀；引人注目的場面","s":"The trial became a media spectacle, and cameras followed the famous singer every time she left the court.","t":"那場審判成了一場媒體奇觀，每次那位知名歌手離開法院時，鏡頭都緊追著她。"},{"w":"subtext","p":"n.","d":"a hidden meaning that is not stated directly","c":"潛台詞；言外之意","s":"The subtext of the advert was that you would be unpopular without the product, so many parents found it unhealthy.","t":"那則廣告的言外之意是沒有這項產品你就不受歡迎，所以許多家長覺得它不健康。"},{"w":"tirade","p":"n.","d":"a long, angry speech criticising someone","c":"激烈的長篇抨擊","s":"The customer posted a long tirade about the hotel, but the manager replied calmly and offered a refund.","t":"那位顧客發了一篇針對飯店的長篇怒罵，但經理冷靜回應並提出退款。"},{"w":"uproar","p":"n.","d":"a lot of public anger or noisy protest","c":"騷動；強烈抗議","s":"There was an uproar when the school banned phones completely, so the principal agreed to discuss the rule with students.","t":"學校全面禁止手機時引起了一片譁然，所以校長同意和學生討論這項規定。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (veracity – verbatim)","cards":[{"w":"veracity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being true","c":"真實性","s":"Reporters questioned the veracity of the photo, because the shadows did not match the time of day.","t":"記者質疑那張照片的真實性，因為陰影和當時的時間對不上。"},{"w":"intent","p":"n.","d":"what someone plans to do","c":"意圖；目的","s":"The intent of the fake account was to make people distrust the election, so the platform deleted it quickly.","t":"那個假帳號的意圖是讓人們不信任選舉，所以平台很快就把它刪除了。"},{"w":"misstep","p":"n.","d":"a mistake in action or judgement","c":"失策；失誤","s":"Posting the joke was a serious misstep for the brand, and it lost thousands of followers in one day.","t":"發布那個笑話是該品牌的嚴重失策，它一天內就失去了數千名追蹤者。"},{"w":"plurality","p":"n.","d":"a large number of different things","c":"多元；多數","s":"A healthy democracy needs a plurality of voices, so it is important that small newspapers can survive too.","t":"健全的民主需要多元的聲音，所以讓小型報社也能生存下去很重要。"},{"w":"slur","p":"n.","d":"an insulting remark about someone","c":"誹謗；侮辱性言語","s":"The fan shouted a racist slur at the player, and the club banned him from the stadium for life.","t":"那位球迷對球員大喊種族歧視的侮辱性言語，球團終身禁止他進入球場。"},{"w":"testimony","p":"n.","d":"a formal statement about what someone saw or knows","c":"證詞","s":"The witness's testimony was very clear, so the jury believed her rather than the man's online supporters.","t":"那位證人的證詞非常清楚，所以陪審團相信她，而不是那名男子的網路支持者。"},{"w":"ethos","p":"n.","d":"the set of beliefs and values of a group","c":"精神；風氣；價值觀","s":"The ethos of the newspaper is to tell the truth without fear, so it often publishes stories that powerful people dislike.","t":"那家報社的精神是無畏地說出真相，所以它常刊登有權勢者不喜歡的報導。"},{"w":"folly","p":"n.","d":"a foolish action or idea","c":"愚蠢；愚行","s":"It would be folly to believe every message in the family group chat, because many of them are forwarded without checking.","t":"相信家族群組裡的每一則訊息是很愚蠢的，因為許多訊息都是未經查證就轉傳的。"},{"w":"impunity","p":"n.","d":"freedom from punishment","c":"不受懲罰","s":"Online trolls often act with impunity, because they hide behind fake names and are rarely caught.","t":"網路酸民常常肆無忌憚，因為他們躲在假名後面，很少被抓到。"},{"w":"mantra","p":"n.","d":"a phrase repeated often as a belief or rule","c":"口頭禪；信條","s":"\"Check before you share\" has become the mantra of our school's media club, and members repeat it at every meeting.","t":"「分享前先查證」已成為我們學校媒體社的信條，社員們每次聚會都會複述。"},{"w":"mockery","p":"n.","d":"laughing at someone in an unkind way","c":"嘲弄；嘲笑","s":"The boy's funny accent became the object of mockery online, so his parents asked the website to remove the video.","t":"那男孩有趣的口音在網路上成了嘲笑的對象，所以他父母要求網站移除影片。"},{"w":"onslaught","p":"n.","d":"a very strong attack or a huge amount of something","c":"猛烈攻擊；大量湧現","s":"The actress faced an onslaught of hateful comments after the film, so she took a break from social media.","t":"電影上映後，那位女演員遭到仇恨留言的猛烈攻擊，所以她暫時停用社群媒體。"},{"w":"taboo","p":"n.","d":"a subject people avoid talking about","c":"禁忌","s":"Mental health used to be a taboo in many families, but now more young people talk about it openly online.","t":"心理健康過去在許多家庭中是禁忌，但現在越來越多年輕人在網路上公開談論。"},{"w":"trepidation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of fear about something that may happen","c":"惶恐；憂慮","s":"She opened the comments under her first video with trepidation, but most of them were kind and encouraging.","t":"她忐忑不安地打開第一支影片下的留言，但大部分都很友善又鼓勵人。"},{"w":"vantage point","p":"n.phr.","d":"a position from which you can see or understand something well","c":"有利位置；觀點","s":"From the vantage point of a small-town reporter, the national news often misses what really matters to local people.","t":"從一位小鎮記者的角度來看，全國新聞常常忽略了對當地人真正重要的事。"},{"w":"purportedly","p":"adv.","d":"according to what is claimed, but possibly not true","c":"據稱；據說","s":"The video purportedly shows a UFO over Taipei, but experts believe it is simply a lantern from a festival.","t":"那段影片據稱拍到台北上空的幽浮，但專家認為那只是節慶放的天燈。"},{"w":"unwittingly","p":"adv.","d":"without knowing or intending","c":"不知不覺地；無意中","s":"Many people unwittingly spread false news, because they share posts from friends without thinking to check them.","t":"許多人不知不覺地散播假新聞，因為他們分享朋友的貼文時沒想到要查證。"},{"w":"ironically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺的是；反諷地","s":"ironically, the talk about the dangers of phones was interrupted when the speaker's own phone started ringing.","t":"諷刺的是，那場談手機危害的講座因講者自己的手機響起而被打斷。"},{"w":"needlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without any good reason","c":"不必要地；無謂地","s":"The headline needlessly frightened parents, because the article said the risk to children was actually very low.","t":"那個標題不必要地嚇壞了家長，因為文章說兒童的風險其實很低。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that everyone can see or hear","c":"公開地","s":"The company publicly apologised for the misleading advert, and it promised to give customers their money back.","t":"那家公司公開為誤導性廣告道歉，並承諾退款給顧客。"},{"w":"wrongly","p":"adv.","d":"in a mistaken or unfair way","c":"錯誤地；冤枉地","s":"The man was wrongly named as the thief on social media, so he received threats even though he was innocent.","t":"那名男子在社群媒體上被誤指為小偷，所以即使他是無辜的，他仍收到威脅。"},{"w":"falsely","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not true","c":"虛假地；不實地","s":"The website falsely claimed that the drink could prevent the flu, so the government ordered it to remove the advert.","t":"那個網站不實地聲稱那款飲料可以預防流感，所以政府命令它撤下廣告。"},{"w":"openly","p":"adv.","d":"without hiding anything","c":"公開地；坦白地","s":"The athlete spoke openly about her anxiety in an interview, and many fans thanked her for being so honest.","t":"那位運動員在訪問中坦率地談論她的焦慮，許多粉絲感謝她如此誠實。"},{"w":"understandably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy to understand","c":"可以理解地","s":"The villagers were understandably angry about the false report, because it had frightened tourists away from their town.","t":"村民們對那則不實報導感到憤怒是可以理解的，因為它把遊客嚇得不敢來他們的小鎮。"},{"w":"verbatim","p":"adv.","d":"using exactly the same words","c":"一字不差地；逐字地","s":"The student copied the article verbatim into his essay, so the teacher noticed immediately that it was not his own work.","t":"那位學生把文章一字不差地抄進他的作文，所以老師立刻注意到那不是他自己寫的。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"go viral","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spread very quickly online","c":"爆紅；瘋傳","s":"Her video of the rescue go viral within hours, and soon TV stations from other countries wanted to interview her.","t":"她的救援影片在幾小時內就爆紅，很快其他國家的電視台都想採訪她。"},{"w":"spread like wildfire","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spread very quickly","c":"迅速蔓延；像野火般傳開","s":"The rumour about the exam spread like wildfire, so by lunchtime every student in the school was talking about it.","t":"關於考試的謠言像野火般迅速傳開，所以到了午餐時間，全校每個學生都在談論它。"},{"w":"with a pinch of salt","p":"phr.","d":"with some doubt, not believing everything","c":"半信半疑地；有所保留地","s":"You should take celebrity diet tips with a pinch of salt, because most stars have personal trainers and chefs.","t":"你應該對名人的減肥秘訣持保留態度，因為大多數明星都有私人教練和廚師。"},{"w":"hit the headlines","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become important news everywhere","c":"登上頭條；成為新聞焦點","s":"The small village hit the headlines when a student found a rare fossil, and tourists began to visit every weekend.","t":"一名學生發現了一塊罕見化石後，那個小村莊登上了頭條，遊客開始每個週末都來參觀。"},{"w":"off the record","p":"phr.","d":"said privately, not to be published","c":"私下說的；不得公開的","s":"The official spoke off the record, so the reporter could use the information but could not print his name.","t":"那位官員是私下透露的，所以記者可以使用這些資訊，但不能刊出他的名字。"},{"w":"word of mouth","p":"n.phr.","d":"information passed from person to person by talking","c":"口耳相傳；口碑","s":"The small café never advertised, but word of mouth brought so many customers that there is always a queue.","t":"那家小咖啡店從不打廣告，但口碑帶來了大量顧客，所以門口總是大排長龍。"},{"w":"behind closed doors","p":"phr.","d":"in private, without the public knowing","c":"私下；閉門","s":"The decision was made behind closed doors, so the public only learned about it after the new rules started.","t":"那項決定是閉門做出的，所以大眾直到新規定開始實施後才得知。"},{"w":"get the message across","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people understand what you mean","c":"把意思傳達清楚","s":"The poster used simple pictures to get the message across, because many of the visitors could not read Chinese.","t":"那張海報使用簡單的圖片來把訊息傳達清楚，因為許多遊客看不懂中文。"},{"w":"beat around the bush","p":"v.phr.","d":"to avoid talking about the main topic","c":"拐彎抹角；說話繞圈子","s":"Please stop beat around the bush and tell me what happened, because I am really worried about you.","t":"請不要再拐彎抹角了，直接告訴我發生了什麼事，因為我真的很擔心你。"},{"w":"read the room","p":"v.phr.","d":"to understand how people around you feel","c":"察言觀色；看場合","s":"The comedian failed to read the room, so he told jokes at a sad event and many guests were offended.","t":"那位喜劇演員沒能察言觀色，所以他在一個哀傷的場合講笑話，許多賓客都覺得被冒犯。"},{"w":"lost in translation","p":"adj.phr.","d":"losing meaning when changed into another language","c":"在翻譯中失去原意","s":"The joke was very funny in Japanese, but most of it was lost in translation, so the English audience did not laugh.","t":"那個笑話在日文裡非常好笑，但大部分在翻譯中失去了原意，所以英語觀眾沒有笑。"},{"w":"the elephant in the room","p":"n.phr.","d":"an obvious problem that nobody wants to talk about","c":"大家避而不談的明顯問題","s":"Everyone discussed the new logo, but nobody mentioned the elephant in the room, which was the company's falling sales.","t":"大家都在討論新標誌，卻沒有人提到那個明擺著卻沒人敢談的問題，也就是公司銷售額下滑。"},{"w":"in a nutshell","p":"phr.","d":"in a few words; briefly","c":"簡而言之；總之","s":"in a nutshell, the report says that most teenagers trust videos more than newspapers, and this worries many teachers.","t":"簡而言之，那份報告說大多數青少年相信影片勝過報紙，而這讓許多老師感到擔憂。"},{"w":"through the grapevine","p":"phr.","d":"through informal talk between people","c":"透過小道消息；輾轉聽說","s":"I heard through the grapevine that our teacher is leaving, but I am not sure whether it is true.","t":"我透過小道消息聽說我們老師要離職了，但我不確定是不是真的。"},{"w":"spill the beans","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell a secret too early","c":"洩露秘密","s":"We planned a surprise party for Mum, but my little brother spill the beans at breakfast, so she knew everything.","t":"我們為媽媽策劃了一場驚喜派對，但我弟弟在早餐時洩露了秘密，所以她全都知道了。"},{"w":"twist one's words","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change the meaning of what someone said","c":"扭曲某人的話","s":"The reporter twist one's words, because I said the plan had problems, not that it was a complete failure.","t":"那位記者扭曲了我的話，因為我說的是那個計畫有問題，不是說它徹底失敗。"},{"w":"out of context","p":"phr.","d":"separated from the situation that explains its meaning","c":"斷章取義；脫離上下文","s":"The clip took her comment out of context, so it sounded rude, although she was actually making a joke.","t":"那段短片把她的評論斷章取義，所以聽起來很無禮，儘管她其實是在開玩笑。"},{"w":"set the record straight","p":"v.phr.","d":"to correct a false story","c":"澄清事實；以正視聽","s":"The singer posted a video to set the record straight, because many fans believed the false rumours about her marriage.","t":"那位歌手發布了一支影片來澄清事實，因為許多粉絲相信了關於她婚姻的不實謠言。"},{"w":"speak one's mind","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say honestly what you think","c":"說出心裡話；直言","s":"Our teacher encourages us to speak one's mind in class discussions, but she also asks us to respect other people's views.","t":"老師鼓勵我們在課堂討論中說出自己的想法，但她也要求我們尊重別人的觀點。"},{"w":"on the same page","p":"adj.phr.","d":"agreeing about what to do","c":"看法一致；有共識","s":"Before the interview, the team met to make sure everyone was on the same page, so nobody gave different answers.","t":"採訪前團隊開了會，確保大家有共識，這樣就不會有人給出不同的答案。"}]}];
